1
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:09,510
Yoko. Yoko.

2
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:14,223
Can I come over to your room?

3
00:00:14,390 --> 00:00:15,850
Or you come to my room?

4
00:00:15,933 --> 00:00:16,767
Sure.

5
00:00:16,851 --> 00:00:17,685
Satoshi!

6
00:00:18,811 --> 00:00:19,812
Either works.

7
00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:23,441
I might want to go to your room.

8
00:00:23,524 --> 00:00:24,775
Sure.

9
00:00:25,151 --> 00:00:26,819
That's cool with me.

10
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:28,946
Kanako!

11
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,656
Normally, you'd invite them to your room.

12
00:00:32,908 --> 00:00:34,076
Welcome.

13
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:37,747
It smells like you.

14
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:38,664
No way.

15
00:00:38,748 --> 00:00:39,665
It smells nice.

16
00:00:39,749 --> 00:00:40,583
Really?

17
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,918
Ew, stop!

18
00:00:43,002 --> 00:00:43,836
He's like a college kid.

19
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:44,754
He said it smells good.

20
00:00:44,837 --> 00:00:45,963
You wanted to talk to me?

21
00:00:46,046 --> 00:00:48,716
Well, to be honest,

22
00:00:49,508 --> 00:00:51,260
I don't have anything specific.

23
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:55,431
Not really.

24
00:00:55,514 --> 00:00:56,515
You don't?

25
00:00:57,808 --> 00:01:00,978
But if I'm being really honest,

26
00:01:01,395 --> 00:01:03,063
I wanted to meet with you.

27
00:01:03,147 --> 00:01:04,440
Thanks.

28
00:01:05,149 --> 00:01:06,901
He said it like he was pumping his brakes.

29
00:01:08,110 --> 00:01:09,028
So,

30
00:01:09,695 --> 00:01:13,991
you know how we went
out to that bar and talked?

31
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:19,497
I had so much fun, and I told you
you should invite me out sometime.

32
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:20,581
I remember.

33
00:01:20,664 --> 00:01:22,208
You do? I see.

34
00:01:22,625 --> 00:01:25,503
I've just been wondering
when I should ask you out.

35
00:01:25,586 --> 00:01:27,213
No way, really?

36
00:01:27,713 --> 00:01:28,798
Really.

37
00:01:29,131 --> 00:01:33,719
I thought that maybe

38
00:01:34,553 --> 00:01:37,097
you forgot or something.

39
00:01:37,181 --> 00:01:38,432
I didn't forget.

40
00:01:38,516 --> 00:01:41,977
It didn't seem like
you were giving it much attention.

41
00:01:42,061 --> 00:01:43,354
I am.

42
00:01:44,814 --> 00:01:45,648
You are?

43
00:01:45,731 --> 00:01:46,774
Yeah.

44
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:49,527
I see.

45
00:01:50,069 --> 00:01:53,989
I'm just thinking how much
of a mystery you are.

46
00:01:54,073 --> 00:01:58,744
I like keeping close to my chest
with the person I'm interested in.

47
00:01:58,828 --> 00:02:00,663
I want to get asked questions.

48
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:03,332
Really? You should just share.

49
00:02:03,415 --> 00:02:04,959
You don't want to?

50
00:02:05,042 --> 00:02:07,127
I want to wait until I'm asked to open up.

51
00:02:07,211 --> 00:02:09,046
I am asking you.

52
00:02:09,964 --> 00:02:11,382
I asked you to open up the other day.

53
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:14,301
You did? Sorry.

54
00:02:14,385 --> 00:02:17,596
I think you're an amazing woman.

55
00:02:18,681 --> 00:02:22,309
Which is why,
I see you as someone really cool, too.

56
00:02:23,310 --> 00:02:26,438
And I see you as a good woman
as a man as well.

57
00:02:26,522 --> 00:02:27,773
Thank you.

58
00:02:27,857 --> 00:02:30,568
It's crazy, but I'm not confessing
my love for you or anything.

59
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:32,820
I didn't think you were.

60
00:02:32,903 --> 00:02:34,113
Good.

61
00:02:34,196 --> 00:02:38,200
So, I wanted to spend some
time alone with you.

62
00:02:38,284 --> 00:02:39,410
So there's no deep meaning.

63
00:02:39,493 --> 00:02:40,828
You know, I'm not the nurturing type.

64
00:02:40,911 --> 00:02:42,162
I didn't think you were.

65
00:02:42,246 --> 00:02:43,455
When you get loud, you're really loud.

66
00:02:43,539 --> 00:02:44,874
Yeah, totally.

67
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:47,877
To be honest, I get preachy.

68
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,295
But for me,

69
00:02:50,629 --> 00:02:52,381
I was careless.

70
00:02:53,591 --> 00:02:55,134
You're cute like a puppy.

71
00:02:55,217 --> 00:02:57,386
-Is she seducing him?
-A puppy?

72
00:02:57,469 --> 00:02:58,554
Satoshi is cute after all.

73
00:02:59,430 --> 00:03:02,808
Not a big dog, more like a toy poodle.

74
00:03:04,143 --> 00:03:05,019
A white one.

75
00:03:05,102 --> 00:03:08,439
Is that because you're underestimating me?

76
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,733
No, you're just totally cute.

77
00:03:12,151 --> 00:03:13,068
I think you're cute.

78
00:03:13,152 --> 00:03:14,028
You do?

79
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,029
Yeah.

80
00:03:15,446 --> 00:03:16,780
Shall we go back together?

81
00:03:16,864 --> 00:03:18,032
Yeah, okay.

82
00:03:18,115 --> 00:03:18,949
Let's go back.

83
00:03:19,033 --> 00:03:20,701
Let's go back together.

84
00:03:20,784 --> 00:03:22,202
Thanks for having me over.

85
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:25,539
Don't mention it.
I need to return this glass.

86
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,082
Let's go.

87
00:03:30,252 --> 00:03:31,337
It's the best.

88
00:03:32,421 --> 00:03:34,590
Where did you go, the lounge?

89
00:03:34,673 --> 00:03:35,633
It's a secret.

90
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:38,510
Sounds a little scandalous.

91
00:03:39,136 --> 00:03:40,512
You went somewhere secret?

92
00:03:40,596 --> 00:03:42,306
Yoko-san is so cool.

93
00:03:42,389 --> 00:03:43,807
She's something.

94
00:03:49,563 --> 00:03:51,440
Everyone is speculating.

95
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,776
They're all speculating so hard.

96
00:04:00,616 --> 00:04:02,159
Everyone is working out.

97
00:04:02,242 --> 00:04:04,453
And doing their morning routines.

98
00:04:06,288 --> 00:04:07,456
Hiroyoshi-san.

99
00:04:07,539 --> 00:04:08,707
He's a dance instructor.

100
00:04:08,791 --> 00:04:09,875
He needs to work out.

101
00:04:09,959 --> 00:04:11,043
True.

102
00:04:11,835 --> 00:04:15,214
Do you do eyelash perms, too?

103
00:04:15,297 --> 00:04:16,423
Yeah.

104
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:21,053
But I don't work on the floor anymore.

105
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:26,225
What I find really strange is that
I couldn't get away from floor at all.

106
00:04:26,308 --> 00:04:30,354
I thought that if I stepped away
from the floor, sales would go down.

107
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:31,271
I get that.

108
00:04:31,355 --> 00:04:34,024
But once I left, it actually went up.

109
00:04:35,818 --> 00:04:37,486
I was like, "Wow!"

110
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:40,030
What are you making?

111
00:04:40,114 --> 00:04:41,824
Some snacks.

112
00:04:41,907 --> 00:04:43,701
-That's amazing.
-You're having wine?

113
00:04:44,493 --> 00:04:46,704
He's making us some yummy finger food.

114
00:04:47,204 --> 00:04:48,664
I'll have some too then.

115
00:04:48,747 --> 00:04:50,541
May I sit next to you?

116
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:51,750
Is someone…

117
00:04:51,834 --> 00:04:53,252
Ice?

118
00:04:53,919 --> 00:04:55,004
What's that?

119
00:04:55,671 --> 00:04:57,256
Shall I get it for you?

120
00:04:58,298 --> 00:05:00,259
Are you listening to me?
Shall I get some for you?

121
00:05:00,342 --> 00:05:01,552
Sure, I'll have some then.

122
00:05:02,553 --> 00:05:03,637
It's really good.

123
00:05:03,721 --> 00:05:04,930
Thank you.

124
00:05:07,224 --> 00:05:10,310
Is anyone going out with anyone tonight?

125
00:05:11,145 --> 00:05:12,771
I'll be here all day.

126
00:05:14,398 --> 00:05:15,607
Where do you want to go?

127
00:05:15,691 --> 00:05:20,404
Was it hard coming straight back
after checking out who was doing it?

128
00:05:20,487 --> 00:05:22,031
Sorry?

129
00:05:23,657 --> 00:05:25,409
Was it that funny?

130
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:27,119
It wasn't funny.

131
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:28,287
It wasn't?

132
00:05:33,083 --> 00:05:35,419
I'd like to go to the lounge
with the two of you.

133
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:36,378
You would?

134
00:05:37,588 --> 00:05:40,799
I probably won't talk.
I'll just sit like this.

135
00:05:40,883 --> 00:05:42,301
That's a bit new.

136
00:05:42,384 --> 00:05:44,762
What, go to the lounge with three people?

137
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:47,931
Who do you think is Hiroyoshi's X?

138
00:05:48,015 --> 00:05:51,435
I've always thought his X is Yoko-san.

139
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:57,232
How is it going today?

140
00:05:57,316 --> 00:05:58,233
Are you having fun?

141
00:05:58,317 --> 00:05:59,485
I am.

142
00:05:59,568 --> 00:06:00,402
You're having fun?

143
00:06:01,153 --> 00:06:05,491
At first, I thought I might want
to go home right away.

144
00:06:06,492 --> 00:06:08,368
But now I want to stay here.

145
00:06:08,452 --> 00:06:09,536
That's great.

146
00:06:09,620 --> 00:06:11,038
That's quick.

147
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:13,290
Good for you.

148
00:06:15,501 --> 00:06:19,963
Having broken up with X,
and getting invited to this hocance,

149
00:06:20,464 --> 00:06:23,092
there were a few things
I thought I had to change.

150
00:06:23,175 --> 00:06:24,718
I want to show her my changed self.

151
00:06:24,802 --> 00:06:26,678
What's that? I'm curious.

152
00:06:26,762 --> 00:06:30,974
So the month before the hocance,

153
00:06:31,058 --> 00:06:34,645
maybe three weeks? I started exercising.

154
00:06:34,728 --> 00:06:35,979
I also stopped drinking alcohol.

155
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:39,233
So I've changed a bit.

156
00:06:39,316 --> 00:06:40,359
Just your appearance?

157
00:06:40,442 --> 00:06:44,530
No, because doing all that
changes your mentality as well.

158
00:06:44,613 --> 00:06:46,281
How did your mentality change?

159
00:06:46,365 --> 00:06:51,245
Now, I wouldn't call it scolding…

160
00:06:51,954 --> 00:06:56,208
but X used to mention how she thought
I might be drinking too much.

161
00:06:56,291 --> 00:06:58,460
And I remembered her saying that.

162
00:06:58,544 --> 00:07:02,506
I was basically drinking every day.

163
00:07:03,382 --> 00:07:04,550
So you cut back?

164
00:07:06,844 --> 00:07:07,928
She's so clearly his X.

165
00:07:08,011 --> 00:07:09,888
-This is just X.
-Just X.

166
00:07:09,972 --> 00:07:11,598
I basically cut my drinking down to zero.

167
00:07:12,975 --> 00:07:16,353
Then I started exercising,

168
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:20,274
and it's fun feeling my body change,
so I like doing push-ups like I did

169
00:07:20,357 --> 00:07:21,900
for the day.

170
00:07:21,984 --> 00:07:24,444
So, wait.

171
00:07:25,112 --> 00:07:28,198
You've just stopped drinking a bit,

172
00:07:28,699 --> 00:07:32,953
and started changing yourself physically?

173
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:37,708
I want my X to see that I'm a catch.

174
00:07:37,791 --> 00:07:39,334
In terms of your appearance?

175
00:07:40,419 --> 00:07:43,088
I suppose nobody can see
what's happening internally.

176
00:07:43,172 --> 00:07:44,298
You can't?

177
00:07:44,381 --> 00:07:47,301
Do you change on the inside that quickly?

178
00:07:47,384 --> 00:07:49,136
But you know…

179
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:52,848
X's words is what made you decide
to cut back on your drinking, right?

180
00:07:52,931 --> 00:07:53,974
That was part of it.

181
00:07:54,057 --> 00:08:00,063
So deciding to cut down
would mean it was an internal change.

182
00:08:00,147 --> 00:08:01,899
That's true.

183
00:08:01,982 --> 00:08:05,152
So did you come hoping for reconciliation?

184
00:08:05,235 --> 00:08:06,236
Of course.

185
00:08:09,072 --> 00:08:12,242
Can I ask what your current ratio is?

186
00:08:12,326 --> 00:08:13,285
Ratio for what?

187
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,536
X or someone else.

188
00:08:15,245 --> 00:08:20,626
I mean, I've said it was 100%
from the very start,

189
00:08:20,709 --> 00:08:27,007
but I think because of my personality,
I convinced myself it had to be 100.

190
00:08:27,090 --> 00:08:28,759
But I've changed to a 50:50 split.

191
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,469
I see.

192
00:08:30,552 --> 00:08:36,099
If I think it's 100%, a part of me
wouldn't let myself look at anyone else.

193
00:08:36,183 --> 00:08:38,894
You are so earnest. Wow.

194
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:42,606
I wonder who made me this way?

195
00:08:42,689 --> 00:08:44,358
You did it yourself.

196
00:08:46,151 --> 00:08:47,945
She's so totally his X.

197
00:08:48,987 --> 00:08:51,156
Look at Kaede-chan's face.

198
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:53,742
I can't say anything to that.

199
00:08:54,493 --> 00:08:59,331
Are you curious what percent
your X is at then?

200
00:09:00,207 --> 00:09:01,583
No, I don't think so.

201
00:09:01,667 --> 00:09:03,126
Why's that?

202
00:09:03,210 --> 00:09:05,837
Before coming here, I told her that

203
00:09:05,921 --> 00:09:10,759
even if it wasn't with me,
I just wanted her to find happiness.

204
00:09:10,842 --> 00:09:12,511
I'm pretty sure everyone's saying that.

205
00:09:12,594 --> 00:09:14,471
Yeah, they all said that.

206
00:09:14,554 --> 00:09:16,807
All the guys are saying that.

207
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:20,352
But we don't really
think like that, do we?

208
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:24,940
When I hear a guy say that, I think,
you're not going to try to make me happy?

209
00:09:25,023 --> 00:09:29,152
We're saying that because if we don't
come with that mindset, it won't work.

210
00:09:29,236 --> 00:09:31,571
Deep down, nobody wants
their X to be taken.

211
00:09:31,655 --> 00:09:35,909
At this age, it's hard to make things work
with only feelings.

212
00:09:40,414 --> 00:09:45,085
I kept thinking that
he was missing the point over and over,

213
00:09:45,168 --> 00:09:49,172
but I was able to gather
that he's been working hard on himself.

214
00:09:49,256 --> 00:09:55,804
I also learned what his mindset
coming into this was.

215
00:09:57,431 --> 00:09:59,516
It just wasn't clicking for me.

216
00:10:01,143 --> 00:10:05,814
Why? I'm sitting here thinking
that he doesn't need to give up.

217
00:10:05,897 --> 00:10:07,566
You're saying I don't need to give up?

218
00:10:07,649 --> 00:10:11,111
I would want you to decide

219
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:16,867
to make the effort in order
to get her to choose you.

220
00:10:17,492 --> 00:10:20,162
Or else it sounds
like you're leaving that to others.

221
00:10:20,245 --> 00:10:22,873
Like the attitude that you're totally fine
as long as she's happy.

222
00:10:22,956 --> 00:10:25,667
It makes it sound like it's all on us.

223
00:10:25,751 --> 00:10:28,879
I hate that the most.

224
00:10:33,842 --> 00:10:35,344
That's unusual.

225
00:10:35,427 --> 00:10:37,971
She reverts to the Kansai dialect with me.

226
00:10:38,055 --> 00:10:42,351
And then she wants to go to the lounge
with me instead of going back to her room?

227
00:10:42,434 --> 00:10:47,939
And when I went,
she kept nitpicking everything I said.

228
00:10:49,024 --> 00:10:51,860
I started to feel apprehensive.

229
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:56,740
All I understood was that she wanted
to let me know she's suffered.

230
00:10:58,533 --> 00:11:01,328
And so today, I thought that
I'll happily take on that role for her.

231
00:11:03,330 --> 00:11:07,209
Watson, I've cracked the case.

232
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:08,794
I felt like Sherlock Holmes.

233
00:11:10,587 --> 00:11:11,797
What is he saying now?

234
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:15,008
Everyone is so possessive.

235
00:11:15,509 --> 00:11:20,097
It means I've come to do my best.

236
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:21,598
Are you trying hard?

237
00:11:23,183 --> 00:11:27,104
Well, that's the tricky thing.

238
00:11:27,187 --> 00:11:31,358
If I pursue my X too much at first,
people would easily figure out who it was.

239
00:11:31,441 --> 00:11:32,734
You know?

240
00:11:33,151 --> 00:11:36,196
If everyone just went for their X,
there would be questions.

241
00:11:36,279 --> 00:11:39,199
But don't you think
everyone's here for reconciliation?

242
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:42,994
I have no idea.

243
00:11:43,078 --> 00:11:46,331
I mean, just because
you're pursuing someone

244
00:11:46,415 --> 00:11:50,877
it might not be your X,
so people might not figure that out.

245
00:11:50,961 --> 00:11:52,671
That's all I was thinking.

246
00:11:53,422 --> 00:11:54,506
I didn't understand.

247
00:11:54,589 --> 00:11:55,465
That's totally fine.

248
00:11:55,549 --> 00:11:56,466
I'm sorry.

249
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,510
It's hard for you.

250
00:12:02,597 --> 00:12:04,266
That was hostile.

251
00:12:04,349 --> 00:12:07,811
What a unique situation.

252
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:10,188
I know I shouldn't be mentioning
gender roles and such,

253
00:12:10,272 --> 00:12:13,984
but being treated
like a small breed of dog

254
00:12:14,067 --> 00:12:16,570
sounds like she's sending
him the message that

255
00:12:16,653 --> 00:12:21,366
she's not seeing him
as a love interest yet.

256
00:12:21,450 --> 00:12:24,911
Well, Satoshi is so straightforward.

257
00:12:24,995 --> 00:12:27,205
He's hoping his feelings
will reach Yoko one day.

258
00:12:27,289 --> 00:12:29,207
You've been pushing Satoshi
this whole time.

259
00:12:29,291 --> 00:12:30,125
He is just…

260
00:12:30,208 --> 00:12:32,711
Kemuri is a stand-up guy.

261
00:12:33,920 --> 00:12:34,838
Exactly.

262
00:12:34,921 --> 00:12:37,215
That's not true, I'm rooting for Satoshi.

263
00:12:37,716 --> 00:12:39,092
And Hiroyoshi.

264
00:12:39,176 --> 00:12:42,512
Consequently, Kanako-san
is definitely feeling irritated.

265
00:12:42,596 --> 00:12:46,433
The thing with Kana-chan
is that she's so unassuming,

266
00:12:46,516 --> 00:12:51,188
she's not the type
to take the initiative to ask him out.

267
00:12:51,271 --> 00:12:53,773
Come on, Satoshi, just reach out to her.

268
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:58,069
You need to go approach
Kanako-san already.

269
00:12:58,153 --> 00:12:59,154
True.

270
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:02,240
But Yoko-san's "It's a secret."

271
00:13:02,324 --> 00:13:03,325
That was so cool.

272
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:04,618
I want to steal that.

273
00:13:04,701 --> 00:13:09,998
True. She's so thoughtful and elegant.

274
00:13:10,081 --> 00:13:12,125
Yes, that was also thoughtful of her.

275
00:13:12,209 --> 00:13:15,629
But actually, when she's talking
with Hiroyoshi,

276
00:13:15,712 --> 00:13:18,673
she seems more like herself.

277
00:13:18,757 --> 00:13:21,927
Which means, it seems like she allows
him in.

278
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:22,844
True.

279
00:13:22,928 --> 00:13:24,679
Like he's special.

280
00:13:24,763 --> 00:13:30,143
So if that's the case, I can see
how Hiroyoshi can still be positive.

281
00:13:30,602 --> 00:13:32,521
Like he's grateful she's engaging him.

282
00:13:32,604 --> 00:13:35,732
"Yoko, go on and explore.
I'm not worried."

283
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:40,487
Yoko is so kind to everyone,
except for me.

284
00:13:40,570 --> 00:13:42,239
Ryo is still around, right?

285
00:13:42,322 --> 00:13:44,658
Yes, he hasn't gone home.

286
00:13:44,741 --> 00:13:45,575
That's good.

287
00:13:45,659 --> 00:13:47,035
Maybe he's going to come up more.

288
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:48,954
It's not like he's going back
to the campgrounds.

289
00:13:49,037 --> 00:13:49,871
That's good.

290
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:54,668
Let's do the shopping tomorrow.

291
00:13:55,961 --> 00:13:57,087
What kind of shopping?

292
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:58,004
We're okay for today?

293
00:13:58,088 --> 00:14:00,465
Is it okay to do the shopping
for Japanese food tomorrow?

294
00:14:00,549 --> 00:14:02,425
What? Japanese food tomorrow?

295
00:14:02,509 --> 00:14:03,969
Yeah, let's do that tomorrow instead.

296
00:14:04,052 --> 00:14:05,136
What about today?

297
00:14:05,262 --> 00:14:06,388
Today…

298
00:14:06,471 --> 00:14:09,057
We'll make something with what we have?

299
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:10,308
Today, you go on a date with me.

300
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,353
For real?

301
00:14:14,187 --> 00:14:15,313
She invited him!

302
00:14:15,397 --> 00:14:16,231
She invited him!

303
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:17,857
Is that okay?

304
00:14:17,941 --> 00:14:19,901
Like now? Or in a bit?

305
00:14:21,778 --> 00:14:22,696
Is that okay?

306
00:14:22,988 --> 00:14:23,905
Good job, Kanako.

307
00:14:24,239 --> 00:14:28,702
One, I'm running out of time
for the hocance.

308
00:14:31,037 --> 00:14:32,038
Also,

309
00:14:32,998 --> 00:14:37,377
the weather looked like
it was going to be clear today,

310
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:43,717
and if he turned me down,
I'll be heartbroken again.

311
00:14:46,428 --> 00:14:47,512
Let's see.

312
00:14:47,596 --> 00:14:51,558
Thanks, Kanako.

313
00:14:52,601 --> 00:14:53,810
I'm surprised you invited me.

314
00:14:53,893 --> 00:14:57,314
I was thinking of asking you out
at least once.

315
00:14:57,439 --> 00:14:59,524
Me?

316
00:14:59,608 --> 00:15:00,442
Of course.

317
00:15:00,525 --> 00:15:02,235
Or just anyone?

318
00:15:02,319 --> 00:15:04,362
I never thought about inviting
anyone else.

319
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:06,906
Really?

320
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:10,785
Did it look like I wanted to go out
on dates with everyone?

321
00:15:11,369 --> 00:15:13,204
But you know,

322
00:15:14,289 --> 00:15:19,127
honestly, I thought you would want someone
new, not me, Kanao.

323
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:20,211
I'm curious about "Kanao."

324
00:15:20,295 --> 00:15:21,129
Kanao.

325
00:15:21,212 --> 00:15:24,257
I thought from the very start
that you would be more interested

326
00:15:24,841 --> 00:15:28,053
in meeting the other four guys

327
00:15:28,136 --> 00:15:31,306
and use your time that way,
if I'm being honest.

328
00:15:31,848 --> 00:15:36,853
What were each of our reasons

329
00:15:38,229 --> 00:15:39,689
for participating in this hocance?

330
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:45,820
For me, it was to reconcile.

331
00:15:46,321 --> 00:15:49,741
I came for you.

332
00:15:50,742 --> 00:15:52,077
-Right?
-At first, yeah.

333
00:15:52,577 --> 00:15:53,662
For me,

334
00:15:54,913 --> 00:15:57,415
I was just really shocked.

335
00:15:57,499 --> 00:16:01,252
And I was surprised how shocked I was.

336
00:16:01,336 --> 00:16:04,047
That I'd actually get hurt.

337
00:16:05,298 --> 00:16:08,301
And I just went a little crazy,
and so did my personality.

338
00:16:08,385 --> 00:16:13,139
I couldn't do anything I wanted
or say anything I wanted.

339
00:16:13,515 --> 00:16:14,974
And I just stopped caring.

340
00:16:15,975 --> 00:16:17,435
I see.

341
00:16:17,519 --> 00:16:20,105
So that's why you kept mentioning
how you were acting.

342
00:16:20,188 --> 00:16:23,233
Yeah, because I was absolutely
furious for a week straight.

343
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:26,778
Maybe I was just overreacting,

344
00:16:26,861 --> 00:16:28,822
but I've been feeling hurt all week.

345
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:39,249
I understand how you might feel
irritated or frustrated

346
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:45,171
at not being able to speak with your X.

347
00:16:45,255 --> 00:16:48,216
But to show that frustration

348
00:16:49,092 --> 00:16:53,304
to the other guys was just something

349
00:16:53,722 --> 00:16:58,643
I had a hard time understanding.

350
00:16:59,686 --> 00:17:05,233
That's why maybe I was acting
colder to you than I should have

351
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:11,114
because of that reaction I had.

352
00:17:13,450 --> 00:17:15,577
So basically, you've lost some
feelings for me.

353
00:17:16,828 --> 00:17:18,997
That's not what I'm trying to say.

354
00:17:19,080 --> 00:17:22,292
More like I had more things
to think about.

355
00:17:24,878 --> 00:17:26,463
I guess we should've talked
about this sooner.

356
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:27,422
You're right.

357
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:29,549
So…

358
00:17:29,632 --> 00:17:32,635
That's true, but time keeps moving.

359
00:17:33,303 --> 00:17:34,929
I bet she wished they did this
on the first day.

360
00:17:36,014 --> 00:17:37,891
Because time keeps moving.

361
00:17:38,516 --> 00:17:41,227
I probably had too high expectations of X.

362
00:17:43,521 --> 00:17:47,108
I came here expecting
he would ask me out more,

363
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:50,737
and generally pursue me more.

364
00:17:52,739 --> 00:17:54,657
That's what I assumed.

365
00:17:55,992 --> 00:18:01,247
He must have lost some interest in me
compared to the beginning.

366
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:08,129
So I thought his feelings for me
are fading.

367
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:12,926
But that's all fair since I did
do something to warrant that reaction.

368
00:18:13,968 --> 00:18:16,596
That's really commendable
how she can criticize herself.

369
00:18:16,679 --> 00:18:18,556
Please don't blame yourself.

370
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:24,771
Are you going to be doing something more

371
00:18:26,231 --> 00:18:28,274
regarding your X?

372
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:31,694
That's a good question.

373
00:18:32,320 --> 00:18:35,073
Who do you think Mao's X is?

374
00:18:35,406 --> 00:18:36,616
I think it's Hikaru.

375
00:18:38,743 --> 00:18:42,622
He definitely has a message for her
in his own way.

376
00:18:43,248 --> 00:18:47,877
That's why I'm hoping I can subtly
give them some advice.

377
00:18:49,128 --> 00:18:51,256
I sometimes wonder if I could have had
a better life.

378
00:18:52,298 --> 00:18:56,386
I even told him to give me back
my life before.

379
00:18:57,637 --> 00:18:59,722
He did say that came as a shock.

380
00:19:00,223 --> 00:19:05,812
But he was also shocked at himself when
he realized he did something that bad.

381
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:09,691
It comes down to how much of a last chance
you're willing to give him.

382
00:19:09,774 --> 00:19:10,942
True.

383
00:19:11,025 --> 00:19:14,529
Whether or not you're willing
to meet him halfway,

384
00:19:14,612 --> 00:19:17,115
or if you just want to sit back
and see what he does.

385
00:19:18,116 --> 00:19:19,284
Really, I want to wait and see.

386
00:19:19,367 --> 00:19:23,371
I want him to just tell me
everything he's thinking.

387
00:19:23,496 --> 00:19:25,999
But he's not the type to do that.

388
00:19:26,082 --> 00:19:29,002
That's right, and I hate that about him.

389
00:19:29,085 --> 00:19:30,086
Hate it.

390
00:19:30,837 --> 00:19:31,671
Seriously.

391
00:19:32,297 --> 00:19:33,256
You love it?

392
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:36,134
Wait, there was a song like that.

393
00:19:36,217 --> 00:19:37,051
Yeah, Morning Musume.

394
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:38,052
Morning Musume?

395
00:19:38,136 --> 00:19:42,557
Wait, sorry, I just derailed everything.

396
00:19:42,640 --> 00:19:44,726
I mean, she set me up!

397
00:19:44,809 --> 00:19:47,312
So, this includes the hocance,

398
00:19:47,979 --> 00:19:50,315
but the story of my life
isn't ending here.

399
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:51,232
Of course.

400
00:19:51,316 --> 00:19:54,652
So even if I don't meet someone here,

401
00:19:54,736 --> 00:19:58,281
I still have plenty of opportunities
to meet men not my X.

402
00:19:58,364 --> 00:19:59,198
That's true.

403
00:19:59,282 --> 00:20:03,328
So part of me thinks there's no reason
to be so fixated on him either.

404
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:06,456
Regarding my X.

405
00:20:06,539 --> 00:20:11,753
Like if he doesn't make any move
to change anything,

406
00:20:11,836 --> 00:20:14,797
then I'm fine cutting ties and ending
things clearly.

407
00:20:14,881 --> 00:20:17,884
Like this is the last shot.
I think that's a good idea.

408
00:20:17,967 --> 00:20:19,719
But there's a contradiction.

409
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:22,013
A contradiction.

410
00:20:22,096 --> 00:20:23,973
He wants to apologize.

411
00:20:25,892 --> 00:20:28,144
But he's waiting for the right timing
for himself.

412
00:20:28,227 --> 00:20:29,187
I see.

413
00:20:29,270 --> 00:20:33,358
But you're left thinking,
why isn't he doing anything?

414
00:20:33,441 --> 00:20:34,609
I see.

415
00:20:34,692 --> 00:20:36,110
That's so lame.

416
00:20:36,194 --> 00:20:37,278
It is.

417
00:20:37,362 --> 00:20:38,237
It's super lame.

418
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:39,948
I feel the same.

419
00:20:40,031 --> 00:20:41,115
It's super lame.

420
00:20:41,199 --> 00:20:45,662
Talking with you guys and seeing men
who are trying to change,

421
00:20:45,745 --> 00:20:48,456
it makes me wonder why he can't.

422
00:20:55,922 --> 00:20:58,216
It's been a while since we saw him.

423
00:20:58,508 --> 00:20:59,968
I laughed.

424
00:21:03,388 --> 00:21:05,765
This looks so good!

425
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:07,266
Right?

426
00:21:07,350 --> 00:21:09,352
Isn't this crazy?

427
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:10,687
What is that, meat?

428
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:11,729
That's crazy.

429
00:21:11,813 --> 00:21:13,147
It looks like high-quality meat.

430
00:21:13,815 --> 00:21:17,568
Is it okay if I boil the offal
that we defrosted yesterday to be safe?

431
00:21:17,652 --> 00:21:18,695
Let's do that.

432
00:21:19,070 --> 00:21:21,864
I suddenly feel motivated,
so I'm jumping into help.

433
00:21:23,574 --> 00:21:25,535
You're making offal stew?

434
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:27,704
I was worried it would go bad.

435
00:21:28,121 --> 00:21:31,624
I just asked my mom for the recipe.

436
00:21:36,629 --> 00:21:39,674
We talk in the Hakata dialect
when it's just the two of us.

437
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:40,842
I have from the start.

438
00:21:40,925 --> 00:21:41,759
Oh, right.

439
00:21:41,843 --> 00:21:43,720
I couldn't hide it anymore
from about the third day.

440
00:21:43,803 --> 00:21:44,637
I get it.

441
00:21:45,096 --> 00:21:48,182
It definitely just came out.

442
00:21:49,308 --> 00:21:50,977
Let's make offal stew again.

443
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:53,104
Yeah? Okay.

444
00:21:55,231 --> 00:21:56,607
Okay, let's make it.

445
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:58,443
Thanks.

446
00:21:59,569 --> 00:22:00,486
I'm happy.

447
00:22:04,282 --> 00:22:06,743
I wonder where everyone is.

448
00:22:06,826 --> 00:22:08,536
They're probably sleeping.

449
00:22:08,619 --> 00:22:10,663
They had about two hours.

450
00:22:10,747 --> 00:22:11,789
A two-hour drama?

451
00:22:11,873 --> 00:22:13,666
Are the usual cooks sleeping too?

452
00:22:14,709 --> 00:22:16,419
There are two of us here.

453
00:22:16,502 --> 00:22:18,171
Really? Mao-chan, too?

454
00:22:18,254 --> 00:22:19,714
Me, Mao-chan, and Yo-chan.

455
00:22:20,089 --> 00:22:20,923
Yo-chan?

456
00:22:21,007 --> 00:22:22,133
Yoko.

457
00:22:22,216 --> 00:22:24,385
I'm pretty sure Yoko
went to go buy something.

458
00:22:24,469 --> 00:22:25,303
A date?

459
00:22:25,386 --> 00:22:26,637
Probably a date.

460
00:22:26,721 --> 00:22:27,972
I see.

461
00:22:28,598 --> 00:22:29,432
Yoko!

462
00:22:29,515 --> 00:22:30,975
-She's not going to eat with us?
-I lost.

463
00:22:31,059 --> 00:22:32,226
Is that the deal?

464
00:22:32,310 --> 00:22:33,644
Did Yoko go out on a date tonight?

465
00:22:33,728 --> 00:22:37,732
I'm just guessing here, but Yoko's
been looking really down lately,

466
00:22:37,815 --> 00:22:41,319
so I think Satoshi invited her out.

467
00:22:41,402 --> 00:22:44,906
That sucks! Looks like we'll be fighting
again today. Goodbye.

468
00:22:47,283 --> 00:22:50,078
Bye. I just made some food just to leave.

469
00:22:51,496 --> 00:22:54,332
Well, Satoshi's a nice guy.

470
00:22:55,374 --> 00:22:57,210
He's considerate.

471
00:23:00,004 --> 00:23:01,923
Kana-chan's expression is just…

472
00:23:03,549 --> 00:23:06,302
Wow.

473
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,638
It's Tokyo Tower.

474
00:23:09,347 --> 00:23:11,557
This is amazing.

475
00:23:11,933 --> 00:23:12,767
Wow.

476
00:23:12,850 --> 00:23:14,644
I bet it's even better at night.

477
00:23:14,727 --> 00:23:15,561
True.

478
00:23:16,729 --> 00:23:19,357
You're not ready to go home, are you?

479
00:23:19,440 --> 00:23:22,318
When he was with Kanako, they were
in some industrial complex.

480
00:23:22,401 --> 00:23:26,864
Yeah, that doesn't seem fair.

481
00:23:27,615 --> 00:23:28,449
Thank you.

482
00:23:28,533 --> 00:23:30,493
Thank you for coming.

483
00:23:30,576 --> 00:23:31,410
Likewise.

484
00:23:32,370 --> 00:23:34,413
Thank you.

485
00:23:34,497 --> 00:23:35,331
Thank you.

486
00:23:35,414 --> 00:23:36,666
Cheers.

487
00:23:38,209 --> 00:23:40,002
The jacket looks great on you.

488
00:23:40,086 --> 00:23:41,879
It suits you.

489
00:23:41,963 --> 00:23:42,797
Really?

490
00:23:43,089 --> 00:23:46,467
Make sure you remember this view.

491
00:23:48,302 --> 00:23:49,137
Please.

492
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:50,221
I'll burn it to my memory.

493
00:23:50,304 --> 00:23:51,639
Please.

494
00:23:52,390 --> 00:23:58,229
I just wanted to know what he liked
about me.

495
00:23:58,312 --> 00:24:01,232
I mean, there's an age gap here.

496
00:24:01,315 --> 00:24:04,902
And Satoshi is really jokey.

497
00:24:04,986 --> 00:24:09,157
He acts like a cat around everyone.

498
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:14,078
So I wanted to ask him today
what he likes about me.

499
00:24:14,745 --> 00:24:20,751
I'm going to be bombarding you with
questions today, so no acting drunk.

500
00:24:21,127 --> 00:24:22,336
Wow.

501
00:24:22,420 --> 00:24:25,590
I see, so he must have pretended
to act drunk before.

502
00:24:26,007 --> 00:24:31,512
Have you ever dated someone who
is divorced with kids?

503
00:24:31,596 --> 00:24:32,889
Yes.

504
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:34,348
And I also

505
00:24:34,432 --> 00:24:35,975
don't really care
about that sort of thing.

506
00:24:36,058 --> 00:24:36,893
You know?

507
00:24:38,603 --> 00:24:41,230
How many are there?

508
00:24:41,314 --> 00:24:43,399
Oh, kids? One.

509
00:24:43,482 --> 00:24:45,776
I have one boy who is all grown up.

510
00:24:46,444 --> 00:24:48,279
He's actually 21.

511
00:24:48,362 --> 00:24:49,530
That's pretty grown!

512
00:24:49,614 --> 00:24:50,907
He runs his own company.

513
00:24:50,990 --> 00:24:52,200
Wow.

514
00:24:52,283 --> 00:24:57,205
So he really has it together.

515
00:25:00,208 --> 00:25:06,214
Obviously, there are things you become
considerate of when kids are involved,

516
00:25:06,881 --> 00:25:10,718
but I don't see it as an obstacle.

517
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:12,637
As long as both parties are fine with it.

518
00:25:13,471 --> 00:25:20,228
I was wondering how things are
between you and your X.

519
00:25:20,686 --> 00:25:22,688
I wanted to ask you that today.

520
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:25,900
So, how are things with you two?

521
00:25:27,360 --> 00:25:30,780
You don't need to choose your
words carefully.

522
00:25:30,863 --> 00:25:31,989
Well.

523
00:25:32,073 --> 00:25:35,493
This is what this date is about, okay? So?

524
00:25:39,330 --> 00:25:40,957
I came to get back together with her.

525
00:25:45,461 --> 00:25:46,629
What about her intentions?

526
00:25:48,965 --> 00:25:54,053
I originally thought that she
wasn't interested at all.

527
00:25:56,472 --> 00:25:57,306
But…

528
00:25:57,390 --> 00:25:58,683
She wasn't.

529
00:25:59,517 --> 00:26:02,561
He just told me he liked me.
He didn't say we were dating.

530
00:26:03,312 --> 00:26:06,857
So he thought you were together,
and so he invited you.

531
00:26:06,941 --> 00:26:08,401
We haven't even held hands.

532
00:26:09,944 --> 00:26:12,196
Despite being the one
invited here by my X,

533
00:26:12,613 --> 00:26:17,326
he doesn't ask me on dates, or
to the lounge, or to the balcony.

534
00:26:17,410 --> 00:26:18,244
Scary.

535
00:26:18,327 --> 00:26:19,829
Like, why did he even invite me here?

536
00:26:19,912 --> 00:26:24,166
I thought he would invite me from
the first day, so I'm over it now.

537
00:26:28,045 --> 00:26:32,550
I'm not really sure

538
00:26:32,633 --> 00:26:35,720
what Kanako-chan is really hoping for,

539
00:26:36,137 --> 00:26:40,516
but I'm also a lot like her.

540
00:26:41,517 --> 00:26:46,230
We both can become really sulky.

541
00:26:47,690 --> 00:26:53,529
But it turned out I was kind of wrong
about that.

542
00:26:56,574 --> 00:27:02,246
However, I discovered a side of her
that's completely different from me.

543
00:27:02,955 --> 00:27:04,332
But let's leave that for now.

544
00:27:04,707 --> 00:27:08,294
Does she actually like me?

545
00:27:08,377 --> 00:27:12,340
Or am I just the only one
she's remotely interested in?

546
00:27:12,882 --> 00:27:16,552
Do you get what I'm trying to say?

547
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:25,561
Why are you suddenly getting so gloomy?

548
00:27:26,187 --> 00:27:27,063
Well,

549
00:27:29,065 --> 00:27:30,649
I don't want to say anything unnecessary.

550
00:27:31,150 --> 00:27:33,652
No? Go ahead, you can say anything.

551
00:27:35,863 --> 00:27:38,991
I didn't know it was so pretty.
Is that a wedding venue?

552
00:27:39,075 --> 00:27:42,745
Yeah, my friend got married here.

553
00:27:42,828 --> 00:27:45,122
Really? It's wonderful.

554
00:27:45,206 --> 00:27:46,540
How was your wedding?

555
00:27:46,624 --> 00:27:47,625
It's Mao-san and Kaede-san.

556
00:27:47,708 --> 00:27:48,709
I had my first child first.

557
00:27:48,793 --> 00:27:49,960
So you had your wedding after.

558
00:27:50,044 --> 00:27:50,878
That's right.

559
00:27:51,462 --> 00:27:54,006
It hadn't been going that well,

560
00:27:54,090 --> 00:27:58,344
then COVID happened the next year.

561
00:27:59,470 --> 00:28:02,014
He used that as the reason
for closing the business.

562
00:28:03,641 --> 00:28:08,229
Then he opened another business
after COVID,

563
00:28:08,729 --> 00:28:12,483
but sales never really took off.

564
00:28:13,484 --> 00:28:18,406
So he went to work every day,
but even if they had customers,

565
00:28:19,031 --> 00:28:23,744
it all got used to pay staff and cover
costs, so nothing was left over for us.

566
00:28:23,828 --> 00:28:25,913
Yeah, it was tough then.

567
00:28:25,996 --> 00:28:31,460
But we didn't split up because
we had no money.

568
00:28:31,961 --> 00:28:36,132
It was tough, but it was during COVID.

569
00:28:36,215 --> 00:28:39,385
We all realized how precious family is,

570
00:28:39,468 --> 00:28:42,721
and how fragile life is.

571
00:28:43,139 --> 00:28:46,851
The world was in chaos.

572
00:28:46,934 --> 00:28:53,315
All we could do was go out
to the grocery store,

573
00:28:53,399 --> 00:28:58,446
but it was a time we were just happy
to eat a warm meal together.

574
00:28:59,697 --> 00:29:03,200
Honestly, I have happy memories
from that period.

575
00:29:04,577 --> 00:29:07,037
And X said the same.

576
00:29:07,413 --> 00:29:09,331
I know it's inappropriate,

577
00:29:09,415 --> 00:29:16,172
but we knew we weren't going
to be living that way forever,

578
00:29:16,255 --> 00:29:20,593
and I think we both realized
how wonderful it was to have a family.

579
00:29:23,637 --> 00:29:27,308
That's when he told me he wanted
to sell the car that was in my name

580
00:29:27,391 --> 00:29:32,855
in order to cover living expenses,

581
00:29:32,938 --> 00:29:35,399
and we did sell it.

582
00:29:36,025 --> 00:29:41,489
I did it because I figured the sooner
we sold it the better,

583
00:29:42,531 --> 00:29:47,703
but he pretty immediately took that money
and went overseas.

584
00:29:50,706 --> 00:29:53,250
Once someone does something
like that to you,

585
00:29:54,168 --> 00:29:58,506
they tend to keep doing it
again and again.

586
00:29:59,256 --> 00:30:02,259
I've actually had a pretty similar
experience to that.

587
00:30:02,343 --> 00:30:05,054
Not with my X,

588
00:30:05,137 --> 00:30:10,226
but someone I lived with quit his job,
and I honestly felt responsible.

589
00:30:10,768 --> 00:30:16,732
We weren't married, and not as close
as you and your X, but we lived together.

590
00:30:17,733 --> 00:30:22,988
Anyway, I told him he could quit
if he wanted to, but it turns out

591
00:30:23,364 --> 00:30:27,326
he borrowed money to pay for the rent
and our living expenses.

592
00:30:27,409 --> 00:30:31,956
At the time, I wondered where the money
came from, but assumed he had savings.

593
00:30:34,542 --> 00:30:37,461
And I was waiting for him to change.

594
00:30:38,337 --> 00:30:42,132
But I didn't say anything. I thought he
would realize and change himself.

595
00:30:45,219 --> 00:30:48,681
That's what I thought,
but you know how timing can be.

596
00:30:48,764 --> 00:30:51,475
Life comes in waves.

597
00:30:51,559 --> 00:30:56,188
I thought he would realize things
himself at his own timing.

598
00:30:56,272 --> 00:31:00,484
I was just working really hard on my own
without bringing any of it up.

599
00:31:00,568 --> 00:31:01,402
Wow.

600
00:31:01,485 --> 00:31:06,574
I thought seeing my hard work would
inspire him, but it didn't work.

601
00:31:07,449 --> 00:31:13,205
Instead, he thought I was completely fine
with the whole situation.

602
00:31:14,373 --> 00:31:19,712
So he took advantage of that,
and didn't work for a year or two.

603
00:31:21,505 --> 00:31:25,968
Which is why I sometimes think

604
00:31:26,302 --> 00:31:30,598
that particular relationship had aspects
that could've been improved upon.

605
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:37,605
But I neglected it, just sitting there
waiting for him to change on his own,

606
00:31:37,688 --> 00:31:40,232
and I learned that that was a mistake.

607
00:31:41,734 --> 00:31:44,528
And in your case,

608
00:31:45,154 --> 00:31:51,327
if there was any part you
could've improved,

609
00:31:51,952 --> 00:31:54,997
then it will help you
in your future relationships.

610
00:31:55,497 --> 00:31:58,876
You can't change the past,

611
00:31:59,668 --> 00:32:03,088
so all you can do is focus on the future.

612
00:32:04,173 --> 00:32:05,674
What is it that you want to do?

613
00:32:05,758 --> 00:32:12,681
I want this trip to help me learn

614
00:32:12,765 --> 00:32:16,644
how to seriously think about my future.

615
00:32:17,645 --> 00:32:18,479
I see.

616
00:32:18,562 --> 00:32:21,732
From what it sounds like,
you came to reconcile.

617
00:32:21,815 --> 00:32:26,987
Which means, it comes down to how you
process what happened in the past.

618
00:32:27,321 --> 00:32:28,656
That's what it boils down to.

619
00:32:30,699 --> 00:32:31,992
I see.

620
00:32:32,076 --> 00:32:35,204
There are still a lot
of unresolved issues.

621
00:32:36,664 --> 00:32:42,086
You know, regarding if you came
for a new love or to get back with your X,

622
00:32:42,169 --> 00:32:45,547
you pretty clearly said you came
to reconcile.

623
00:32:45,631 --> 00:32:50,052
But I didn't come here to get back
with my X.

624
00:32:51,387 --> 00:32:54,348
That's not my goal.

625
00:32:54,431 --> 00:33:00,688
Honestly, I more or less came here
for closure.

626
00:33:00,771 --> 00:33:04,066
I see.

627
00:33:04,149 --> 00:33:08,862
But he's saying he came here
to get back together with me,

628
00:33:09,988 --> 00:33:11,240
that's what he told me.

629
00:33:14,576 --> 00:33:16,495
Meaning, he's interested in it.

630
00:33:16,578 --> 00:33:18,205
Are there any other players in the game?

631
00:33:19,123 --> 00:33:24,545
The others are more like friends.

632
00:33:25,546 --> 00:33:26,630
Am I not a friend?

633
00:33:26,714 --> 00:33:29,174
You don't feel like a friend.

634
00:33:30,718 --> 00:33:33,220
It's hard to not think of you as a man.

635
00:33:35,723 --> 00:33:36,807
Because I'm a man.

636
00:33:36,890 --> 00:33:40,602
I think you're the most masculine
out of everyone.

637
00:33:41,353 --> 00:33:44,189
In that case, you might be
the most feminine.

638
00:33:44,273 --> 00:33:47,443
Me, really?

639
00:33:47,526 --> 00:33:51,196
Yuck, you can't just say that in return.

640
00:33:52,072 --> 00:33:55,159
Setting that aside, aren't they
a great match?

641
00:33:55,409 --> 00:33:56,243
For sure.

642
00:33:56,326 --> 00:33:57,494
You know.

643
00:33:57,995 --> 00:34:00,372
I think I said I came here
to get back with my X.

644
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:03,167
Yes, that's what you said.

645
00:34:03,584 --> 00:34:07,379
I had a lot of things to think about.

646
00:34:07,463 --> 00:34:10,382
And in conclusion…

647
00:34:10,466 --> 00:34:12,384
You have an answer now?

648
00:34:12,468 --> 00:34:13,719
Well,

649
00:34:14,136 --> 00:34:19,558
I want to cherish the time
I spend with you.

650
00:34:22,269 --> 00:34:25,105
So I'm really happy you invited me out.

651
00:34:25,189 --> 00:34:26,398
I'm enjoying this moment.

652
00:34:28,859 --> 00:34:29,693
So this is a good thing?

653
00:34:30,402 --> 00:34:31,487
Of course.

654
00:34:31,570 --> 00:34:33,405
But why?

655
00:34:34,406 --> 00:34:35,866
What's so good about me?

656
00:34:37,701 --> 00:34:41,079
I'm the type of person

657
00:34:41,163 --> 00:34:45,459
who wants to know these things.

658
00:34:46,835 --> 00:34:49,379
You're the first one

659
00:34:50,088 --> 00:34:54,510
who tried to get to know me
on a personal level.

660
00:34:57,137 --> 00:35:03,852
When I asked what motivated you
to be so positive,

661
00:35:03,936 --> 00:35:10,108
it really resonated with me when you said
it was your employees.

662
00:35:10,192 --> 00:35:13,654
I'm happy you remembered.

663
00:35:15,155 --> 00:35:16,490
I think that's what I like.

664
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:19,743
This isn't a lie.

665
00:35:20,744 --> 00:35:21,912
That's why I was happy for today.

666
00:35:21,995 --> 00:35:24,581
Thank you.

667
00:35:27,459 --> 00:35:28,710
I had a ton of fun.

668
00:35:29,670 --> 00:35:33,799
My impression of him just had
a huge positive shift.

669
00:35:36,176 --> 00:35:38,095
I bet she likes being pursued.

670
00:35:38,178 --> 00:35:40,264
I think I was wrong.

671
00:35:40,347 --> 00:35:43,433
He remembered that I said that
instead of something happening to me,

672
00:35:43,517 --> 00:35:48,146
I'm a lot happier when the important
people around me

673
00:35:48,272 --> 00:35:54,570
are the ones who experience good things,

674
00:35:54,653 --> 00:35:56,488
and that's like my dream.

675
00:35:57,030 --> 00:36:01,702
And when he told me he liked that,
it really hit me.

676
00:36:02,452 --> 00:36:03,871
I was a little taken aback.

677
00:36:04,246 --> 00:36:06,707
I think my face turned beet red.

678
00:36:07,124 --> 00:36:10,210
I was really embarrassed thinking
how red I was.

679
00:36:11,211 --> 00:36:12,170
Wow.

680
00:36:16,300 --> 00:36:21,680
While this is a crucial time for the kids,

681
00:36:22,306 --> 00:36:26,894
I think they're past the age
when they really need a father.

682
00:36:26,977 --> 00:36:28,729
No, I think kids will always need a dad.

683
00:36:28,812 --> 00:36:29,646
You think so?

684
00:36:29,730 --> 00:36:33,150
My parents divorced when I was little.

685
00:36:33,233 --> 00:36:34,484
Oh, really?

686
00:36:35,277 --> 00:36:41,408
And I grew up not knowing my dad,
and always wanted a father figure.

687
00:36:41,491 --> 00:36:42,326
I see.

688
00:36:42,409 --> 00:36:43,243
Yeah.

689
00:36:43,327 --> 00:36:46,914
My mom had bad legs,

690
00:36:46,997 --> 00:36:50,000
and I grew up feeling like
I had to protect women.

691
00:36:50,584 --> 00:36:53,712
Which is why I became pretty
independent at a young age.

692
00:36:53,795 --> 00:36:54,713
I see.

693
00:36:54,796 --> 00:37:00,218
I can't really rely on my family, I almost
never asked for anything.

694
00:37:00,302 --> 00:37:04,514
And eventually, the only people I could
really be vulnerable with were men.

695
00:37:04,598 --> 00:37:05,474
Like my boyfriends.

696
00:37:05,557 --> 00:37:07,142
I see.

697
00:37:07,225 --> 00:37:10,395
And I always sought a father figure
in people like that.

698
00:37:11,021 --> 00:37:12,522
I see.

699
00:37:13,815 --> 00:37:17,277
Your kids may think they have to believe
they don't need a father,

700
00:37:17,361 --> 00:37:20,530
for your sake.

701
00:37:20,614 --> 00:37:22,366
It's felt that way.

702
00:37:24,326 --> 00:37:26,870
My oldest is a boy.

703
00:37:27,329 --> 00:37:29,539
He should be in his rebellious phase now,

704
00:37:29,623 --> 00:37:35,796
but he's not because I think he wants
to protect his mother.

705
00:37:35,879 --> 00:37:38,006
He's always been so considerate.

706
00:37:39,424 --> 00:37:43,679
He even sent me off to this,
wishing me luck.

707
00:37:43,762 --> 00:37:46,974
Of course I call him,
and we send each other texts.

708
00:37:48,308 --> 00:37:52,229
So they've had to endure things
other family's don't,

709
00:37:52,896 --> 00:37:58,193
since they basically didn't have
a dad around.

710
00:37:58,777 --> 00:38:00,988
And they might never have one around.

711
00:38:04,992 --> 00:38:10,956
I think my son has felt like he didn't
need a dad as long as I was around.

712
00:38:11,039 --> 00:38:13,041
And that's something X's noticed too,

713
00:38:13,792 --> 00:38:17,379
and he feels bad for not being around.

714
00:38:17,921 --> 00:38:22,467
But he says he wants to spend
more time with them,

715
00:38:22,551 --> 00:38:27,097
and that he wants the two of us
to raise the kids together.

716
00:38:27,931 --> 00:38:31,893
Wanting to see them grow together more,

717
00:38:33,103 --> 00:38:35,313
I think it's definitely a key point.

718
00:38:35,981 --> 00:38:38,316
I think so.

719
00:38:42,112 --> 00:38:43,447
Right.

720
00:38:45,615 --> 00:38:50,370
Sounds like Mao-san is keeping the door
open for Hikaru-san.

721
00:38:50,454 --> 00:38:53,790
She said it was 15 percent, but it feels
like it's gone up.

722
00:38:54,833 --> 00:38:57,294
I think it's more than 15.

723
00:38:57,377 --> 00:39:01,673
Hearing them talk, it feels
like it's gone up.

724
00:39:01,757 --> 00:39:06,470
She did appreciate having the family
together during COVID.

725
00:39:06,553 --> 00:39:08,263
It's not like they never got along.

726
00:39:08,346 --> 00:39:13,268
Just the things he did at the end
that really cornered her

727
00:39:13,351 --> 00:39:17,230
were just too painful.

728
00:39:17,314 --> 00:39:19,858
But maybe now…

729
00:39:20,192 --> 00:39:23,945
Perhaps part of her is thinking,
'if only that didn't happen."

730
00:39:24,321 --> 00:39:29,117
I know it defeats the whole point, but
I think everyone should just reconcile.

731
00:39:29,701 --> 00:39:30,911
I want all of them to reconcile.

732
00:39:30,994 --> 00:39:32,621
You do?

733
00:39:32,704 --> 00:39:36,625
In Kanako and Satoshi's case,
they'd be dating for the first time.

734
00:39:37,626 --> 00:39:38,794
It wouldn't be reconciliation.

735
00:39:38,877 --> 00:39:39,920
That's not a transit.

736
00:39:40,003 --> 00:39:41,588
Not a transit.

737
00:39:41,671 --> 00:39:43,173
Or getting back together.

738
00:39:43,256 --> 00:39:46,551
So, that's not the end to the night.

739
00:39:46,635 --> 00:39:49,471
Apparently, a huge incident
is about to happen.

740
00:39:49,554 --> 00:39:50,472
What?

741
00:39:50,555 --> 00:39:52,099
Sit back and watch.

742
00:39:52,182 --> 00:39:53,600
Cheers.

743
00:39:55,018 --> 00:39:55,852
Are you getting hit?

744
00:39:57,479 --> 00:40:00,440
Honestly, I've been
getting hit constantly.

745
00:40:00,524 --> 00:40:04,569
I like you, and you're the only one
I can be honest with.

746
00:40:06,113 --> 00:40:09,407
So the person who seems to be my X

747
00:40:10,033 --> 00:40:12,828
tends to completely ignore me when
we're in a group.

748
00:40:13,328 --> 00:40:16,123
She doesn't touch me.

749
00:40:16,206 --> 00:40:17,874
I've noticed that this whole time.

750
00:40:19,167 --> 00:40:22,087
Every time she does, I think,
oh, we're doing this again.

751
00:40:23,380 --> 00:40:28,677
A lot of the girls are much more open,
including me into their conversation.

752
00:40:28,760 --> 00:40:29,719
Yeah.

753
00:40:29,803 --> 00:40:31,179
But she doesn't do that with me at all.

754
00:40:31,263 --> 00:40:32,097
I see.

755
00:40:32,180 --> 00:40:36,810
But then again,

756
00:40:37,435 --> 00:40:41,231
if I make the wrong move,
it would really change the dynamic.

757
00:40:41,815 --> 00:40:47,612
I've been spending this hocance wondering
what to do about it.

758
00:40:47,696 --> 00:40:50,407
I think she's been relying on you
the whole time.

759
00:40:50,490 --> 00:40:55,829
If I'm being harsh, I think your X
has been relying on you.

760
00:40:55,912 --> 00:40:56,746
Maybe.

761
00:40:56,830 --> 00:40:59,833
Someone who is so good at her job,

762
00:40:59,916 --> 00:41:03,253
suddenly starts acting like
she's in fifth grade.

763
00:41:03,336 --> 00:41:05,881
I can't help but think it's because
she likes you.

764
00:41:05,964 --> 00:41:10,844
Yeah, so deep down, I'm actually feeling
pretty happy.

765
00:41:10,927 --> 00:41:14,431
The way she acts just with me,
makes me think she really likes me.

766
00:41:14,514 --> 00:41:15,432
You know?

767
00:41:15,515 --> 00:41:17,142
Yeah, I don't blame you.

768
00:41:17,225 --> 00:41:18,059
Yeah.

769
00:41:18,602 --> 00:41:21,771
She treats me like she would family.

770
00:41:22,814 --> 00:41:27,611
So I told her, don't you think you're
being too cold to me?

771
00:41:27,986 --> 00:41:30,989
But X was well aware of that,

772
00:41:31,072 --> 00:41:33,241
and she told me her mom says
the same thing to her.

773
00:41:33,325 --> 00:41:38,163
So in that sense, I feel
I'm like family in her eyes.

774
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:43,043
It gives me confidence.

775
00:41:45,128 --> 00:41:50,967
I've built such a solid relationship
with her, and that gives me confidence.

776
00:41:51,051 --> 00:41:54,804
I realized that during this hocance.

777
00:41:54,888 --> 00:41:56,598
I think that's good.

778
00:41:56,681 --> 00:42:01,102
It wasn't until this hocance that
I realized I'm in the realm of family.

779
00:42:01,186 --> 00:42:02,896
So I feel like I still have a shot.

780
00:42:02,979 --> 00:42:04,147
I can turn things around.

781
00:42:04,231 --> 00:42:05,357
Like you can keep going.

782
00:42:05,774 --> 00:42:09,527
I was so happy to realize
how much she relies on me.

783
00:42:09,611 --> 00:42:11,071
Yeah.

784
00:42:11,571 --> 00:42:14,908
Well, she's being treated like
a woman in Azabudai right now.

785
00:42:14,991 --> 00:42:16,743
By a man 11 years her junior.

786
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:28,213
Who is it? They came back?
Is this going to cause some waves?

787
00:42:28,296 --> 00:42:29,756
Yeah.

788
00:42:29,839 --> 00:42:30,715
Is it the huge incident?

789
00:42:30,799 --> 00:42:31,633
Plus, they're drunk.

790
00:42:39,266 --> 00:42:40,225
See!

791
00:42:40,308 --> 00:42:41,935
This is going to be bad.

792
00:42:42,018 --> 00:42:43,770
Welcome back.

793
00:42:43,853 --> 00:42:47,649
We've been waiting for you.

794
00:42:47,732 --> 00:42:49,401
There's nobody here!

795
00:42:50,110 --> 00:42:50,944
Yeah.

796
00:42:51,027 --> 00:42:52,279
What were you doing?

797
00:42:52,779 --> 00:42:53,738
Welcome back, Yoko.

798
00:42:55,323 --> 00:42:56,157
Thanks.

799
00:42:56,241 --> 00:42:57,534
Both of them?

800
00:42:57,617 --> 00:42:58,868
What were you doing?

801
00:42:58,952 --> 00:43:01,371
Did you go eat French food
dressed like that?

802
00:43:02,622 --> 00:43:04,457
Is that French?

803
00:43:04,541 --> 00:43:05,500
Italian?

804
00:43:05,583 --> 00:43:06,626
Either French or Italian.

805
00:43:06,710 --> 00:43:08,253
I think it's French.

806
00:43:08,336 --> 00:43:10,463
It's French, not Italian.

807
00:43:10,547 --> 00:43:12,257
You guys look like you're dressed for it.

808
00:43:12,340 --> 00:43:13,174
Want to drink?

809
00:43:14,009 --> 00:43:14,968
Sure.

810
00:43:15,051 --> 00:43:16,720
I think I'll go back to my room.

811
00:43:17,846 --> 00:43:20,265
Seriously, I want no part of this today.

812
00:43:20,348 --> 00:43:21,725
Where did everyone go?

813
00:43:22,100 --> 00:43:23,727
I'm done for today.

814
00:43:23,810 --> 00:43:25,145
Everyone is doing whatever.

815
00:43:27,063 --> 00:43:28,148
Did Yoko-san just…?

816
00:43:28,231 --> 00:43:29,441
They're in all different places?

817
00:43:29,524 --> 00:43:31,026
I'm going back.

818
00:43:31,693 --> 00:43:32,902
Good night, Kanako.

819
00:43:32,986 --> 00:43:33,945
Good night.

820
00:43:34,029 --> 00:43:35,488
Kana-chan's big mad.

821
00:43:35,572 --> 00:43:36,865
She's pretty mad.

822
00:43:36,948 --> 00:43:38,241
That's not good.

823
00:43:38,783 --> 00:43:39,617
I see.

824
00:43:42,203 --> 00:43:43,330
Bad timing, huh?

825
00:43:43,413 --> 00:43:44,664
No.

826
00:43:44,748 --> 00:43:45,874
No?

827
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:49,836
Is it Hiro?

828
00:43:52,172 --> 00:43:53,006
What's wrong, Kanako?

829
00:43:53,465 --> 00:43:55,383
Do you need something to drink?

830
00:43:55,467 --> 00:43:56,384
I'm good for tonight.

831
00:43:56,468 --> 00:43:58,345
What happened? Did they get back?

832
00:43:58,428 --> 00:44:03,391
Yeah. Apparently, Yoko and Satoshi
had dinner at a French restaurant.

833
00:44:03,475 --> 00:44:05,185
They were dressed really sharp.

834
00:44:06,519 --> 00:44:08,438
I'm not planning on going back
to the living room.

835
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:11,608
I just stormed out of there.

836
00:44:11,691 --> 00:44:12,525
For real?

837
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:17,238
Maybe you should go talk
to Kanako, Satoshi.

838
00:44:17,322 --> 00:44:19,616
But she went back to her room, right?

839
00:44:20,241 --> 00:44:21,910
Yeah, but…

840
00:44:21,993 --> 00:44:24,204
But hold on.

841
00:44:24,287 --> 00:44:26,623
I don't know who invited who out,

842
00:44:27,040 --> 00:44:31,336
but from Satoshi's point of view,
he just had dinner with you,

843
00:44:31,419 --> 00:44:35,632
and maybe he's in a really good mood
from the time you spent together.

844
00:44:35,715 --> 00:44:38,510
I don't see any reason why he should go

845
00:44:38,635 --> 00:44:42,514
and comfort Kanako.

846
00:44:42,806 --> 00:44:46,976
I was just trying to think
of what Kanako wants you to do.

847
00:44:47,060 --> 00:44:48,937
That's your kindness.

848
00:44:49,020 --> 00:44:51,523
Actually, it's because I'm a lot like her.

849
00:44:51,648 --> 00:44:58,029
I think she wants Satoshi to go see her.

850
00:44:59,656 --> 00:45:01,199
That might be true.

851
00:45:01,282 --> 00:45:02,659
I know it's meddling,

852
00:45:02,742 --> 00:45:05,662
I'm just saying that that's what I think
she wants.

853
00:45:05,745 --> 00:45:07,705
But you should just do whatever you want.

854
00:45:07,789 --> 00:45:09,499
Exactly.

855
00:45:10,458 --> 00:45:12,377
Friendship is important,

856
00:45:12,669 --> 00:45:15,713
but we didn't come here to make friends.

857
00:45:17,715 --> 00:45:20,093
I'm not worried about Kanako
because of friendship,

858
00:45:20,176 --> 00:45:23,012
I'm just concerned for her as a person.

859
00:45:23,513 --> 00:45:26,850
If you keep worrying about people
like that…

860
00:45:27,308 --> 00:45:28,226
I'm back.

861
00:45:28,309 --> 00:45:30,854
Welcome back. Can we talk?

862
00:45:30,979 --> 00:45:32,021
Sure.

863
00:45:33,898 --> 00:45:34,941
Where?

864
00:45:35,024 --> 00:45:36,234
Is outside okay?

865
00:45:36,317 --> 00:45:37,235
Outside?

866
00:45:37,318 --> 00:45:42,532
Geez, Satoshi, what are you mulling over
so hard?

867
00:45:42,615 --> 00:45:45,785
Sorry.

868
00:45:48,538 --> 00:45:50,790
Yoko doesn't know how I feel, right?

869
00:45:51,249 --> 00:45:54,419
What are your feelings?

870
00:45:55,336 --> 00:45:57,547
I didn't really talk to Yoko.

871
00:46:00,675 --> 00:46:03,011
Good morning.

872
00:46:03,553 --> 00:46:05,472
Dad's here.

873
00:46:05,555 --> 00:46:06,806
Fatherhood has entered the room.

874
00:46:06,890 --> 00:46:07,724
The teacher's arrived.

875
00:46:12,103 --> 00:46:14,522
I'm furious right now.

876
00:46:15,607 --> 00:46:17,066
Uncle.

877
00:46:17,150 --> 00:46:18,234
I'm absolutely furious.

878
00:46:19,235 --> 00:46:21,779
I'm so pissed right now,
I need you to go punch them for me.

879
00:46:22,614 --> 00:46:23,573
Punch who?

880
00:46:23,656 --> 00:46:25,074
The guy and the girl.

881
00:46:26,409 --> 00:46:27,410
Who and who?

882
00:46:28,161 --> 00:46:30,997
Everyone in the living room
except Hika-chan.

883
00:46:31,706 --> 00:46:33,875
This is total chaos.

884
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:35,793
What for? What are you mad about?

885
00:46:37,337 --> 00:46:38,588
That they went on a date?

886
00:46:38,671 --> 00:46:40,965
Yeah, I didn't like that.

887
00:46:42,342 --> 00:46:45,720
I could handle it if it were
like a cafe or a park date.

888
00:46:45,803 --> 00:46:47,931
Why is it that he goes to such
nice places with her?

889
00:46:48,014 --> 00:46:50,266
When I didn't even get dinner last night.
I was starving.

890
00:46:51,684 --> 00:46:53,228
I told him.

891
00:46:53,561 --> 00:46:56,231
See, I was right about her being unhappy
with her dock location.

892
00:46:56,314 --> 00:46:57,357
There's the dock incident.

893
00:46:57,440 --> 00:46:58,608
She feels treated differently.

894
00:46:58,691 --> 00:47:01,027
He's always wearing a suit.

895
00:47:01,110 --> 00:47:01,986
He was in a suit?

896
00:47:02,070 --> 00:47:02,904
Yeah.

897
00:47:03,404 --> 00:47:05,448
That totally turned me off.

898
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:07,242
I don't want to talk to him anymore.

899
00:47:08,076 --> 00:47:10,662
I want to leave the hocance.

900
00:47:12,497 --> 00:47:13,623
This is pretty bad.

901
00:47:15,458 --> 00:47:16,626
Uncle, help.

902
00:47:18,711 --> 00:47:20,463
Go ahead and vent if you want.

903
00:47:20,797 --> 00:47:24,050
It's not like I think him and Yoko are
going to end up together.

904
00:47:25,134 --> 00:47:27,720
But I don't like what the two of them
are doing.

905
00:47:28,763 --> 00:47:33,393
I think Yoko is wanting to flaunt it
in front of Hiro.

906
00:47:33,476 --> 00:47:35,186
Right.

907
00:47:35,270 --> 00:47:37,063
I don't want her using him
for that either.

908
00:47:37,146 --> 00:47:39,440
I think that's a separate thing.
Not that I know.

909
00:47:40,400 --> 00:47:43,820
But Yoko's talking to the wrong guy
for that. He's too young.

910
00:47:44,487 --> 00:47:47,407
There's no way he could solve
any of her concerns.

911
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:48,700
She should be asking you out.

912
00:47:50,243 --> 00:47:52,161
Why pick such a younger guy?

913
00:47:52,245 --> 00:47:54,330
She should be inviting out Uncle!

914
00:47:55,373 --> 00:47:57,625
The one with the most experience.

915
00:47:57,709 --> 00:47:58,543
I can't.

916
00:47:58,626 --> 00:47:59,836
Maybe she had a reason for that.

917
00:47:59,919 --> 00:48:00,878
I'm sure she does.

918
00:48:00,962 --> 00:48:03,423
Well, then give me the reason already,
I'm waiting.

919
00:48:03,506 --> 00:48:04,424
You are so mad.

920
00:48:04,507 --> 00:48:05,758
It's like tell me already.

921
00:48:05,842 --> 00:48:06,884
You're so mad.

922
00:48:06,968 --> 00:48:08,428
You mean from Satoshi?

923
00:48:09,220 --> 00:48:11,806
You should just ask him directly.
"What's going on?"

924
00:48:11,889 --> 00:48:14,309
He was actually mulling something over
just now.

925
00:48:15,018 --> 00:48:16,311
Satoshi was?

926
00:48:16,394 --> 00:48:19,772
You should go tell him what he's supposed
to do in this situation.

927
00:48:19,856 --> 00:48:21,149
To be more like you.

928
00:48:22,734 --> 00:48:24,068
"Be more like me."

929
00:48:24,193 --> 00:48:25,528
Tell him, "Be a good guy like me."

930
00:48:25,612 --> 00:48:27,280
I haven't done anything.

931
00:48:27,989 --> 00:48:30,450
I don't think I'm that good
of a guy either.

932
00:48:30,533 --> 00:48:35,038
You're the most mature, the most balanced,
and the most reliable.

933
00:48:35,121 --> 00:48:36,956
Then why don't you go out on
a date with him tomorrow.

934
00:48:38,124 --> 00:48:39,208
That's true.

935
00:48:39,292 --> 00:48:41,544
-Ask her out.
-You want to?

936
00:48:43,671 --> 00:48:45,548
Why do you look so reluctant?

937
00:48:45,632 --> 00:48:46,883
No, no, I would.

938
00:48:46,966 --> 00:48:47,800
You look reluctant.

939
00:48:47,884 --> 00:48:49,260
I would like to go with you.

940
00:48:49,886 --> 00:48:52,805
Kaede is so good at handling
the situation so skillfully!

941
00:48:52,889 --> 00:48:55,642
If she turns out to be his X, that's
impressive telling him to ask her out.

942
00:48:55,725 --> 00:48:58,353
I think she's his X.

943
00:48:58,436 --> 00:49:01,230
You should just unload everything
on Satoshi.

944
00:49:01,522 --> 00:49:02,940
He won't say it.

945
00:49:03,024 --> 00:49:07,236
Even when I'm this furious, he just
keeps everything vague.

946
00:49:07,737 --> 00:49:11,407
What did you talk about on your
date with him last night?

947
00:49:11,491 --> 00:49:13,034
The date last night?

948
00:49:13,117 --> 00:49:18,039
I said I didn't want him going out with
other girls, and I'd do the same.

949
00:49:18,122 --> 00:49:20,124
You actually said that?

950
00:49:21,125 --> 00:49:22,043
That's cute.

951
00:49:22,126 --> 00:49:22,960
Yeah.

952
00:49:23,044 --> 00:49:24,921
That's really impressive you were
able to say that.

953
00:49:25,004 --> 00:49:25,838
Wow.

954
00:49:27,382 --> 00:49:28,800
I keep getting asked out on dates.

955
00:49:28,883 --> 00:49:29,717
You mean yesterday.

956
00:49:29,801 --> 00:49:31,344
So I literally don't have the time.

957
00:49:31,427 --> 00:49:34,180
You wouldn't ever turn them down?

958
00:49:34,263 --> 00:49:35,556
Right, I forgot you're a pushover.

959
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:38,267
Honestly, it was difficult
to turn her down.

960
00:49:38,351 --> 00:49:42,855
I couldn't tell her I wouldn't go.

961
00:49:42,939 --> 00:49:44,023
It's not in your personality.

962
00:49:44,107 --> 00:49:47,777
Are you able to say that then
in the same situation?

963
00:49:47,860 --> 00:49:49,153
I know how to say no.

964
00:49:49,237 --> 00:49:50,613
For real?

965
00:49:51,656 --> 00:49:52,573
You seem sure about that.

966
00:49:52,657 --> 00:49:53,491
Yup.

967
00:49:57,495 --> 00:50:01,290
So then

968
00:50:01,374 --> 00:50:06,254
I'm still your main choice?

969
00:50:06,337 --> 00:50:08,965
That hasn't changed, even now?

970
00:50:09,966 --> 00:50:10,800
For real?

971
00:50:13,469 --> 00:50:15,346
Don't forget, they never dated.

972
00:50:15,847 --> 00:50:16,681
That's true.

973
00:50:16,764 --> 00:50:17,724
That's right.

974
00:50:17,932 --> 00:50:19,016
That's amazing.

975
00:50:19,100 --> 00:50:21,144
Because he's the one who invited me.

976
00:50:22,228 --> 00:50:24,564
I came because I thought he liked me.

977
00:50:27,608 --> 00:50:30,778
Like today, he worked hard to peel
the boiled eggs.

978
00:50:31,571 --> 00:50:35,032
So I thought that was a sudden change.

979
00:50:35,116 --> 00:50:37,618
I was happy when I saw him
put in the effort.

980
00:50:37,702 --> 00:50:41,664
Then he goes to a French restaurant
which is clearly better.

981
00:50:41,914 --> 00:50:45,877
And that turned me off.

982
00:50:46,294 --> 00:50:47,253
You really like him.

983
00:50:47,336 --> 00:50:49,630
It's really not about that.

984
00:50:49,714 --> 00:50:52,592
I came here thinking I wanted
to develop feelings for him,

985
00:50:52,675 --> 00:50:54,343
but now I've changed my mind.

986
00:50:54,427 --> 00:50:56,387
That's where I'm at.

987
00:50:57,263 --> 00:51:00,183
Does it feel like he's been taken away?

988
00:51:00,266 --> 00:51:02,059
No, I don't he will

989
00:51:02,143 --> 00:51:04,812
since I doubt he'll end up with Yoko.

990
00:51:04,896 --> 00:51:06,773
So I know that.

991
00:51:06,856 --> 00:51:10,359
I'm guessing either he or Yoko just wanted
to discuss something or get advice.

992
00:51:10,777 --> 00:51:13,029
I didn't like the French restaurant bit,
and his appearance.

993
00:51:14,071 --> 00:51:14,989
Right.

994
00:51:15,072 --> 00:51:18,701
He was dressed like that when he went
to the bar with Yoko, too.

995
00:51:19,786 --> 00:51:22,622
So maybe he likes Yoko.

996
00:51:23,372 --> 00:51:25,666
I think that's a possibility.

997
00:51:25,750 --> 00:51:29,045
That's like the rule for this hocance.

998
00:51:29,128 --> 00:51:33,090
If that's the case, I want to leave
because why did I even come here?

999
00:51:36,886 --> 00:51:40,473
Since half my experience here
is just painful,

1000
00:51:41,182 --> 00:51:44,227
like what kind of guy puts you through
this much pain?

1001
00:51:44,310 --> 00:51:48,397
You wouldn't do that to someone
you cared about, right, Uncle?

1002
00:51:48,940 --> 00:51:51,734
Right, but why don't you just
move on from him then?

1003
00:51:52,276 --> 00:51:54,362
You came because you thought
he liked you, right?

1004
00:51:54,445 --> 00:51:56,405
But his actions are suggesting otherwise.

1005
00:51:57,198 --> 00:51:59,116
Then why don't you spend time with
someone else?

1006
00:51:59,617 --> 00:52:01,118
You're really fixated on only him.

1007
00:52:01,953 --> 00:52:06,874
Then there must be a different way
of doing things, in my opinion.

1008
00:52:08,459 --> 00:52:11,003
This is Love Transit, after all.

1009
00:52:11,087 --> 00:52:15,091
Well, I came here without thinking
about that too much,

1010
00:52:17,552 --> 00:52:18,511
so I'm confused.

1011
00:52:18,594 --> 00:52:19,470
It seems that way.

1012
00:52:19,554 --> 00:52:22,056
I didn't give this enough thought.
What a blunder.

1013
00:52:22,515 --> 00:52:23,850
That's totally fine.

1014
00:52:23,933 --> 00:52:24,934
Just…

1015
00:52:25,017 --> 00:52:28,271
It's fine to feel irritated, but the fact
that you feel that way

1016
00:52:28,354 --> 00:52:30,189
means you were interested in him.

1017
00:52:30,273 --> 00:52:33,609
You seem set on just waiting.

1018
00:52:33,693 --> 00:52:37,738
It sounds to me like you want him to take
responsibility for bringing you here.

1019
00:52:37,822 --> 00:52:38,656
I told him that.

1020
00:52:39,115 --> 00:52:42,410
I told him I'd like to talk with him
every day

1021
00:52:42,493 --> 00:52:45,538
and just share what happened.

1022
00:52:45,621 --> 00:52:47,915
But he won't take action.

1023
00:52:48,666 --> 00:52:50,042
Then just move on then.

1024
00:52:50,126 --> 00:52:51,377
Is what we end up thinking.

1025
00:52:51,460 --> 00:52:52,628
We haven't even talked about it.

1026
00:52:52,712 --> 00:52:54,630
Why don't you ask him that then?

1027
00:52:55,631 --> 00:52:57,633
So go back to the living room
or call him here.

1028
00:52:57,717 --> 00:52:58,551
Right.

1029
00:52:58,634 --> 00:52:59,468
Let's call him here.

1030
00:52:59,552 --> 00:53:00,803
It'll be easier to talk that way.

1031
00:53:00,887 --> 00:53:01,721
Go call him over!

1032
00:53:01,804 --> 00:53:02,763
That's a good idea.

1033
00:53:04,098 --> 00:53:05,141
Who did she just order?

1034
00:53:05,224 --> 00:53:06,767
It's Uncle!

1035
00:53:06,851 --> 00:53:08,394
Go on.

1036
00:53:08,811 --> 00:53:10,521
Kaede is the commander.

1037
00:53:10,605 --> 00:53:13,107
That was a crazy way to give an order.

1038
00:53:13,190 --> 00:53:15,610
Why did they break up? I want to know!

1039
00:53:16,652 --> 00:53:19,572
You also need the courage not to go.

1040
00:53:20,114 --> 00:53:22,366
You didn't come here to appease her.

1041
00:53:22,783 --> 00:53:26,495
You'd also be giving her false hope,
you know?

1042
00:53:28,080 --> 00:53:31,000
Hikaru is giving a big speech.

1043
00:53:31,500 --> 00:53:33,711
She could invite you.

1044
00:53:35,004 --> 00:53:36,672
Satoshi.

1045
00:53:36,756 --> 00:53:39,342
I just got myself dragged into
a whole thing.

1046
00:53:39,425 --> 00:53:40,259
Are you okay?

1047
00:53:40,343 --> 00:53:41,761
He got dragged in?

1048
00:53:41,844 --> 00:53:42,678
That's so true.

1049
00:53:42,762 --> 00:53:43,596
For real.

1050
00:53:43,679 --> 00:53:44,513
Definitely.

1051
00:53:45,723 --> 00:53:49,769
We basically concluded that you two
should just talk.

1052
00:53:51,437 --> 00:53:55,566
Look, I get that you just
got dragged into it,

1053
00:53:55,650 --> 00:53:57,276
but I don't think it's anyone
else's business.

1054
00:53:57,360 --> 00:53:58,527
Absolutely.

1055
00:53:58,611 --> 00:54:01,864
Is someone waiting?

1056
00:54:01,948 --> 00:54:02,782
Yes, in the lounge.

1057
00:54:03,032 --> 00:54:03,866
I see.

1058
00:54:03,950 --> 00:54:06,786
If there's something
you want to talk about,

1059
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:11,916
you also have the choice
to tell her what you're feeling.

1060
00:54:11,999 --> 00:54:12,917
I agree.

1061
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:17,797
And for me, if you don't have anything
to talk about,

1062
00:54:17,880 --> 00:54:20,383
then you don't have to bother.

1063
00:54:23,678 --> 00:54:24,637
Right.

1064
00:54:24,720 --> 00:54:29,809
But this could be a good opportunity.

1065
00:54:29,892 --> 00:54:34,021
It's not easy to create an opportunity
to say how you feel.

1066
00:54:34,105 --> 00:54:37,108
Because people are usually worried
about offending others.

1067
00:54:37,191 --> 00:54:42,446
You should go talk to her
if you have anything to say.

1068
00:54:42,822 --> 00:54:43,656
Thanks.

1069
00:54:43,739 --> 00:54:44,615
Thank you, Uncle.

1070
00:54:44,740 --> 00:54:45,574
Uncle!

1071
00:54:45,658 --> 00:54:48,828
What do you actually think though?
You don't know?

1072
00:54:48,911 --> 00:54:50,538
Honestly,

1073
00:54:51,414 --> 00:54:54,917
thinking about it now,

1074
00:54:55,751 --> 00:55:01,340
maybe I haven't really made myself
clear to her.

1075
00:55:03,551 --> 00:55:10,099
I think this is a sign from her
asking me to tell her.

1076
00:55:11,183 --> 00:55:15,479
I feel like I should go.

1077
00:55:15,563 --> 00:55:18,941
Then you should go. It's that simple.

1078
00:55:19,025 --> 00:55:20,985
You're right.

1079
00:55:22,820 --> 00:55:27,616
Part of me doesn't want to go,
but I'll do my best.

1080
00:55:27,700 --> 00:55:29,869
Okay, I'll bring the other two back here.

1081
00:55:29,952 --> 00:55:30,995
Thank you.

1082
00:55:31,078 --> 00:55:32,663
Dai-chan, sorry. And thanks.

1083
00:55:35,791 --> 00:55:39,045
You don't need to try hard or anything,
but good luck.

1084
00:55:40,421 --> 00:55:44,300
I'll try my best not to try too hard.

1085
00:55:45,801 --> 00:55:47,094
Thanks.

1086
00:55:47,178 --> 00:55:48,179
Have a good one.

1087
00:55:50,598 --> 00:55:51,432
It's Uncle.

1088
00:55:51,515 --> 00:55:52,391
He's coming, so let's go.

1089
00:55:53,392 --> 00:55:54,977
Why? Stay here.

1090
00:55:55,061 --> 00:55:56,187
You have to do this one-on-one.

1091
00:55:56,270 --> 00:55:57,480
No! I can't!

1092
00:55:57,563 --> 00:55:58,397
Just talk it out.

1093
00:55:58,481 --> 00:55:59,774
Stay here, Coach.

1094
00:55:59,857 --> 00:56:01,442
No. Let's go.

1095
00:56:01,901 --> 00:56:03,819
Or else, he probably won't come here.

1096
00:56:03,903 --> 00:56:04,737
No?

1097
00:56:04,820 --> 00:56:08,032
Right, he hates that sort of thing.
I knew that.

1098
00:56:08,115 --> 00:56:10,618
He hates it when people talk about him.

1099
00:56:10,701 --> 00:56:14,747
I also think you should be having
this talk alone.

1100
00:56:16,749 --> 00:56:19,085
But I have nothing to say.

1101
00:56:19,168 --> 00:56:20,169
Just say what you told us.

1102
00:56:21,170 --> 00:56:22,797
It's basically what I told him yesterday.

1103
00:56:22,880 --> 00:56:25,382
So ask him why he met with Yoko
despite what you talked about.

1104
00:56:25,466 --> 00:56:26,300
Exactly.

1105
00:56:28,094 --> 00:56:29,053
I just don't know.

1106
00:56:29,136 --> 00:56:32,973
Hold on, do you want to talk to him
or not? Because I'll go stop him.

1107
00:56:33,599 --> 00:56:35,810
No, please call him here. I'm sorry.

1108
00:56:35,893 --> 00:56:36,727
Good for you.

1109
00:56:36,811 --> 00:56:37,645
Then we should go.

1110
00:56:37,728 --> 00:56:38,771
Yes.

1111
00:56:40,231 --> 00:56:41,816
Stay calm.

1112
00:56:41,899 --> 00:56:42,942
I can't.

1113
00:56:43,484 --> 00:56:46,320
I'll come check on you later.

1114
00:56:48,030 --> 00:56:49,115
Just wait for me, okay?

1115
00:56:50,407 --> 00:56:51,867
I'll have some water.

1116
00:56:52,660 --> 00:56:53,786
Just try to stay calm.

1117
00:57:01,252 --> 00:57:02,628
Thanks.

1118
00:57:03,212 --> 00:57:04,046
Uncle's so impressive.

1119
00:57:04,130 --> 00:57:06,757
He's so kind, holding the door
open for them.

1120
00:57:09,218 --> 00:57:11,303
-Just tell her how you feel.
-Right.

1121
00:57:11,387 --> 00:57:12,221
Thank you.

1122
00:57:12,304 --> 00:57:13,139
Do it right, okay?

1123
00:57:18,018 --> 00:57:21,063
If he doesn't want to talk to her,
it seems he's not that into her.

1124
00:57:21,147 --> 00:57:23,190
Or he feels guilty.

1125
00:57:30,197 --> 00:57:31,157
He should just go in.

1126
00:57:32,158 --> 00:57:32,992
Satoshi?

1127
00:57:33,075 --> 00:57:34,160
Is he going to run away?

1128
00:57:34,660 --> 00:57:35,703
He froze.

1129
00:57:35,786 --> 00:57:36,620
No way.

1130
00:57:37,663 --> 00:57:39,415
Wait, no way.

1131
00:57:39,498 --> 00:57:41,959
I bet he's already drunk.

1132
00:57:42,042 --> 00:57:45,754
Maybe he's thinking about talking
in the morning? There's no sleeping now.

1133
00:57:45,838 --> 00:57:48,215
He knows she's going to yell at him.

1134
00:57:48,299 --> 00:57:49,800
And it's just a pain.

1135
00:57:51,886 --> 00:57:52,887
Thank goodness.

1136
00:57:52,970 --> 00:57:53,804
He went in.

1137
00:57:53,888 --> 00:57:54,763
Thank goodness.

1138
00:57:54,847 --> 00:57:57,683
It looks like he's preparing himself
to get scolded.

1139
00:57:57,766 --> 00:57:58,726
The principal's office.

1140
00:58:08,110 --> 00:58:09,403
Hey.

1141
00:58:12,615 --> 00:58:13,782
Did you have fun?

1142
00:58:16,285 --> 00:58:19,580
The view was nice.

1143
00:58:21,582 --> 00:58:22,458
I see.

1144
00:58:24,210 --> 00:58:25,502
You didn't want to say it?

1145
00:58:26,128 --> 00:58:28,255
I wasn't sure if it was okay to tell you.

1146
00:58:28,881 --> 00:58:30,841
Since it's not just about me.

1147
00:58:31,717 --> 00:58:36,513
I can't tell you everything,
I don't even know all of it.

1148
00:58:37,139 --> 00:58:39,391
Did you want to go on the date
after she asked you?

1149
00:58:44,939 --> 00:58:46,815
You can go ahead and be honest.

1150
00:58:48,359 --> 00:58:50,027
I'm totally fine.

1151
00:58:53,906 --> 00:58:54,823
Yeah.

1152
00:58:57,993 --> 00:58:59,995
I think I did.

1153
00:59:00,329 --> 00:59:02,289
I do think she's a great woman.

1154
00:59:02,831 --> 00:59:05,918
So I guess you don't see me
as an option then.

1155
00:59:08,545 --> 00:59:10,631
I wouldn't say that.

1156
00:59:11,465 --> 00:59:16,595
Nothing is ever just 100 or 0.

1157
00:59:18,305 --> 00:59:23,310
I'm spending my days
just thinking about that.

1158
00:59:24,645 --> 00:59:27,439
You know what I mean?

1159
00:59:28,941 --> 00:59:34,822
You said you wanted to find new love
when we first reunited.

1160
00:59:36,407 --> 00:59:39,034
And I've been operating under
that assumption.

1161
00:59:39,118 --> 00:59:39,952
I see.

1162
00:59:40,828 --> 00:59:42,454
That was big.

1163
00:59:43,247 --> 00:59:44,081
Yeah.

1164
00:59:53,632 --> 00:59:55,509
This hocance is draining.

1165
00:59:55,968 --> 00:59:58,470
Yeah, it's tough for everyone.

1166
00:59:58,554 --> 01:00:04,560
So honestly, I do understand how you feel.

1167
01:00:05,060 --> 01:00:09,398
But I wish you would've pushed through
and stayed instead of leaving the room.

1168
01:00:09,481 --> 01:00:11,400
Well, I've been waiting for you all day.

1169
01:00:11,483 --> 01:00:13,193
I thought we'd be having dinner together.

1170
01:00:13,736 --> 01:00:15,362
I even made offal stew.

1171
01:00:15,446 --> 01:00:17,865
I asked my mom this afternoon
for the recipe.

1172
01:00:19,325 --> 01:00:23,787
I was looking forward to eating it
with you, but you didn't come back.

1173
01:00:24,455 --> 01:00:30,419
Then when I saw that you were
dressed for a French restaurant,

1174
01:00:31,420 --> 01:00:36,508
it made me sad since you just
took me to a park yesterday.

1175
01:00:36,592 --> 01:00:38,969
So I couldn't bear it anymore.

1176
01:00:40,054 --> 01:00:41,513
That's how I felt, honestly.

1177
01:00:42,806 --> 01:00:44,767
Do you understand where I'm coming from?

1178
01:00:45,142 --> 01:00:46,477
I do, of course.

1179
01:00:46,560 --> 01:00:47,519
Right?

1180
01:00:48,812 --> 01:00:51,648
I understand, but…

1181
01:00:51,732 --> 01:00:56,278
It would've been fine if it were
just the two of us.

1182
01:00:56,362 --> 01:00:59,448
I wanted Yoko to know how I felt.

1183
01:01:00,491 --> 01:01:04,328
Why is that?

1184
01:01:04,411 --> 01:01:06,747
Why is it necessary for you to tell her
how you feel?

1185
01:01:07,247 --> 01:01:08,707
What's the purpose of that?

1186
01:01:08,791 --> 01:01:10,000
I told you yesterday.

1187
01:01:11,377 --> 01:01:13,295
That I wanted you to turn down
any date invitations.

1188
01:01:14,588 --> 01:01:16,882
Although I'm sure you went
because you wanted to.

1189
01:01:16,965 --> 01:01:18,467
Yeah,

1190
01:01:19,426 --> 01:01:22,554
but I'm not just living for myself.

1191
01:01:25,516 --> 01:01:30,562
I've never just done whatever I felt like,
not even when I was a kid.

1192
01:01:31,313 --> 01:01:36,402
I admire people who can understand
how others feel and think.

1193
01:01:37,403 --> 01:01:42,991
In that sense, I feel like you're
not like that in that respect.

1194
01:01:44,493 --> 01:01:46,537
I'm sorry for telling you this so late.

1195
01:01:49,123 --> 01:01:53,460
I noticed how differently you behave
compared to me.

1196
01:01:53,544 --> 01:01:59,508
There were lots of things I saw
that I wouldn't do.

1197
01:02:00,175 --> 01:02:04,304
The reaction you had today would be
perfectly fine if it was just me there.

1198
01:02:05,514 --> 01:02:07,099
I mean, I wanted to punch Yoko.

1199
01:02:07,516 --> 01:02:08,725
That's not right, though.

1200
01:02:09,518 --> 01:02:14,231
Yoko has gone through a lot in her life.

1201
01:02:14,606 --> 01:02:16,191
You'd do the same in my shoes.

1202
01:02:16,275 --> 01:02:18,652
No way! That's what I'm talking about.

1203
01:02:21,155 --> 01:02:22,739
I'm telling you this because I wouldn't.

1204
01:02:23,240 --> 01:02:24,533
But if you were me…

1205
01:02:24,616 --> 01:02:27,453
I won't. I'd never do that.

1206
01:02:27,995 --> 01:02:29,496
That's why I'm telling you.

1207
01:02:33,959 --> 01:02:35,794
It's okay to cry.

1208
01:02:36,670 --> 01:02:40,215
It's okay to ask me to step out
and talk one on one.

1209
01:02:40,632 --> 01:02:44,386
I thought you were the kind of person
who could take actions like that.

1210
01:02:45,637 --> 01:02:48,599
And I think you are.

1211
01:02:49,057 --> 01:02:52,561
But with the way you behaved,

1212
01:02:52,644 --> 01:02:54,855
I mean Hika-chan and Yoko
are both really kind.

1213
01:02:54,938 --> 01:02:56,565
I'm not trying to overly praise them,

1214
01:02:56,648 --> 01:02:58,025
and I'm not trying to bad-mouth you.

1215
01:02:58,108 --> 01:03:03,906
I just want you to realize something like
that would happen given the situation.

1216
01:03:08,827 --> 01:03:10,621
I can see Satoshi's point.

1217
01:03:10,704 --> 01:03:13,457
It's a bit complicated.

1218
01:03:13,540 --> 01:03:14,625
Don't blame her.

1219
01:03:14,708 --> 01:03:19,338
I'm sure getting yelled at
would make anyone sad.

1220
01:03:24,176 --> 01:03:29,890
After you left, Hika-chan explained to me
the whole situation.

1221
01:03:29,973 --> 01:03:31,934
Yeah, because I'd been waiting.

1222
01:03:32,017 --> 01:03:35,062
And even I understand that.

1223
01:03:35,145 --> 01:03:37,731
You could've just not gone on that date.

1224
01:03:52,788 --> 01:03:56,124
Look, I know I'm the one at fault.

1225
01:03:58,377 --> 01:04:00,045
Participating in this show,

1226
01:04:01,838 --> 01:04:03,549
I'm surprised

1227
01:04:05,259 --> 01:04:06,843
by how little I can seem to endure.

1228
01:04:09,638 --> 01:04:11,598
Sorry.

1229
01:04:13,642 --> 01:04:14,643
I'm sorry.

1230
01:04:15,310 --> 01:04:16,645
You don't need to apologize.

1231
01:04:16,728 --> 01:04:20,774
This is just how I am.

1232
01:04:22,109 --> 01:04:24,528
I'm trying hard to change.

1233
01:04:25,112 --> 01:04:27,823
But sometimes I can't bear it.

1234
01:04:33,620 --> 01:04:34,788
I'm Kanako.

1235
01:04:35,497 --> 01:04:38,667
I want to fully enjoy the hocance,

1236
01:04:39,251 --> 01:04:45,549
and have a nice fling, even
if it doesn't lead to a relationship.

1237
01:04:47,467 --> 01:04:50,679
I don't really have much romantic
experience to speak of.

1238
01:04:52,055 --> 01:04:54,099
I haven't been in many relationships.

1239
01:04:54,182 --> 01:04:55,017
Really?

1240
01:04:55,100 --> 01:04:56,351
Which is why…

1241
01:04:57,311 --> 01:04:59,104
I barely have any dating experience!

1242
01:05:00,981 --> 01:05:02,357
Maybe three?

1243
01:05:02,774 --> 01:05:07,613
I was so busy working in my 20s.

1244
01:05:08,822 --> 01:05:10,699
I would wake up at 4:00 a.m.

1245
01:05:11,325 --> 01:05:13,994
and work until late,

1246
01:05:15,245 --> 01:05:19,458
so I really didn't have time for dating.

1247
01:05:21,043 --> 01:05:24,129
She went to an all girls' school.

1248
01:05:24,212 --> 01:05:26,923
Amid her busy life after
starting her first job,

1249
01:05:27,007 --> 01:05:30,761
the person she met
in her hometown of Fukuoka was…

1250
01:05:37,601 --> 01:05:39,269
He messaged me

1251
01:05:40,062 --> 01:05:44,232
when I was feeling really negative
from a heartbreak.

1252
01:05:45,442 --> 01:05:48,445
I had really pushed everyone away
at that point,

1253
01:05:48,528 --> 01:05:50,822
turning down many invitations.

1254
01:05:50,906 --> 01:05:54,284
If he would've pushed a bit more,
I definitely would've gone for it.

1255
01:05:54,368 --> 01:05:55,619
Timing-wise as well.

1256
01:05:57,454 --> 01:05:59,122
I've never had a food tour date.

1257
01:06:00,123 --> 01:06:02,250
In your life?

1258
01:06:02,334 --> 01:06:03,710
Really?

1259
01:06:04,336 --> 01:06:05,295
No?

1260
01:06:05,379 --> 01:06:06,880
You can do it.

1261
01:06:06,963 --> 01:06:07,798
Down the hatch.

1262
01:06:12,052 --> 01:06:12,886
Yum.

1263
01:06:12,969 --> 01:06:14,388
It's not too hot?

1264
01:06:14,471 --> 01:06:15,681
It's not hot?

1265
01:06:15,764 --> 01:06:16,598
Is it good?

1266
01:06:16,723 --> 01:06:20,227
It was so fun eating soup dumplings
together, wasn't it?

1267
01:06:20,310 --> 01:06:21,144
It was fun.

1268
01:06:21,228 --> 01:06:22,521
It was really fun, right?

1269
01:06:22,604 --> 01:06:24,981
Because you can't do that in the hotel.

1270
01:06:25,065 --> 01:06:26,942
Eating out like that.

1271
01:06:28,318 --> 01:06:30,862
It was really fun and exciting.

1272
01:06:32,114 --> 01:06:36,243
What was it that I did that changed
you like that?

1273
01:06:37,661 --> 01:06:39,454
Maybe your date with Mao-chan?

1274
01:06:40,831 --> 01:06:41,790
I didn't like it.

1275
01:06:42,499 --> 01:06:46,044
Having her go out on a date with you
before me.

1276
01:06:46,628 --> 01:06:48,046
Seeing you to go out.

1277
01:06:49,005 --> 01:06:53,510
I haven't really spent
that much time with you.

1278
01:06:54,636 --> 01:06:59,474
I'd like to talk to you more,
even just in the living room.

1279
01:07:00,058 --> 01:07:01,351
Yeah.

1280
01:07:01,893 --> 01:07:05,814
So I don't feel like I need to go out
on dates with any of the other guys.

1281
01:07:08,942 --> 01:07:13,655
The reason I participated in this hocance?

1282
01:07:16,158 --> 01:07:17,659
I wrote it in my letter.

1283
01:07:27,961 --> 01:07:31,006
Hello, nice to meet you.

1284
01:07:31,089 --> 01:07:32,632
Hello.

1285
01:07:39,014 --> 01:07:43,894
Satoshi-san is very calm, kind,
and slightly shy person.

1286
01:07:45,937 --> 01:07:49,608
I'm curious about what he thinks of me
right now.

1287
01:07:50,984 --> 01:07:55,989
If possible, I might be happy if he
pursued me a bit more proactively.

1288
01:08:01,411 --> 01:08:04,956
I hope that through this hocance,

1289
01:08:05,040 --> 01:08:09,211
we're able to learn more about each other.

1290
01:08:10,712 --> 01:08:15,050
I look forward to spending time
with Satoshi-san.

1291
01:08:22,224 --> 01:08:24,392
She wrote all that in her letter?

1292
01:08:24,476 --> 01:08:25,769
I see.

1293
01:08:25,852 --> 01:08:28,188
She was totally sending him an invitation.

1294
01:08:31,942 --> 01:08:36,363
I came here because I wanted to learn
how you felt about me.

1295
01:08:37,656 --> 01:08:40,450
Do you actually like me?

1296
01:08:40,534 --> 01:08:45,038
Or not really?
That's what I came to find out.

1297
01:08:52,337 --> 01:08:54,297
I don't know either.

1298
01:08:55,423 --> 01:09:00,554
What is it that makes you think I'm good?

1299
01:09:02,180 --> 01:09:04,724
Or maybe there really isn't anyone good,
if you think about it.

1300
01:09:08,353 --> 01:09:12,232
From my point of view,
I'm not really getting any vibes

1301
01:09:13,608 --> 01:09:15,735
that you like me.

1302
01:09:16,695 --> 01:09:19,072
In that respect,

1303
01:09:20,699 --> 01:09:24,661
Yoko's actually shared her feelings
with me.

1304
01:09:26,162 --> 01:09:31,334
And I feel like I can't ignore
those feelings.

1305
01:09:31,418 --> 01:09:32,419
I see.

1306
01:09:32,961 --> 01:09:35,088
So you're interested in Yoko.

1307
01:09:38,300 --> 01:09:43,680
I do think that the time we spend
together is important,

1308
01:09:44,598 --> 01:09:45,849
so I went with her today.

1309
01:09:49,769 --> 01:09:50,729
Okay.

1310
01:09:51,396 --> 01:09:52,564
Thank you for telling me.

1311
01:09:56,526 --> 01:09:57,527
I've been rejected.

1312
01:09:58,445 --> 01:10:00,655
That's not what I meant.

1313
01:10:01,031 --> 01:10:01,865
It's fine.

1314
01:10:06,036 --> 01:10:09,789
I'm shocked. He didn't like me after all.

1315
01:10:11,333 --> 01:10:12,334
Isn't that messed up?

1316
01:10:13,376 --> 01:10:17,297
So I guess he's more interested
in Yoko now.

1317
01:10:18,214 --> 01:10:23,803
I'm left feeling like why did you
invite me here?

1318
01:10:27,849 --> 01:10:29,643
Ow.

1319
01:10:29,726 --> 01:10:31,436
Why?

1320
01:10:31,519 --> 01:10:35,523
Kanako and Satoshi finally sat down
and had a proper conversation.

1321
01:10:35,607 --> 01:10:42,238
I was watching the whole time thinking
"What are you doing, Satoshi."

1322
01:10:42,322 --> 01:10:47,494
But objectively speaking,
this is Love Transit.

1323
01:10:47,577 --> 01:10:50,664
If you think about the context
of this project,

1324
01:10:50,747 --> 01:10:54,918
he's free to fall for Yoko even though
he started off interested in Kanako.

1325
01:10:55,001 --> 01:10:56,169
That's part of the show.

1326
01:10:56,252 --> 01:10:58,838
So if you remain neutral,

1327
01:10:58,922 --> 01:11:02,801
it's not like Satoshi did anything wrong.

1328
01:11:02,884 --> 01:11:06,179
It just looks a little complicated

1329
01:11:07,472 --> 01:11:10,558
because of this ex-boyfriend
and ex-girlfriend history.

1330
01:11:10,642 --> 01:11:11,476
Right.

1331
01:11:11,559 --> 01:11:15,814
If you look at it objectively, Satoshi
is playing Love Transit properly.

1332
01:11:15,897 --> 01:11:17,023
He's loving freely.

1333
01:11:17,107 --> 01:11:18,316
Yeah, he's loving freely.

1334
01:11:18,400 --> 01:11:22,904
If you notice in the beginning,
he fell for Yoko at first sight.

1335
01:11:22,988 --> 01:11:23,822
I see.

1336
01:11:23,905 --> 01:11:27,409
Before participating, he thought he'd
be with Kanako-san,

1337
01:11:27,492 --> 01:11:33,373
which is why he wants to create reasons
why she's not the one for him.

1338
01:11:33,498 --> 01:11:37,836
But things became so hectic
for Uncle there.

1339
01:11:39,004 --> 01:11:44,467
I'm shocked they call him Uncle.

1340
01:11:44,551 --> 01:11:45,719
"Go do it for me, Uncle."

1341
01:11:45,802 --> 01:11:47,595
He's pretty young.

1342
01:11:47,679 --> 01:11:49,264
He's 43.

1343
01:11:49,347 --> 01:11:50,223
He's just 43.

1344
01:11:50,306 --> 01:11:52,434
They treat him like a butler.

1345
01:11:52,517 --> 01:11:54,686
Kaede is just issuing him orders.

1346
01:11:56,354 --> 01:11:57,188
Just with her finger.

1347
01:11:57,272 --> 01:11:58,440
They think he's a concierge.

1348
01:11:58,523 --> 01:11:59,441
The commander.

1349
01:12:00,108 --> 01:12:02,569
I think Daichi's stock
within the Love Transit cast

1350
01:12:02,652 --> 01:12:06,364
and with the panel

1351
01:12:06,448 --> 01:12:07,699
is just skyrocketing.

1352
01:12:07,782 --> 01:12:09,451
I bet they all love him.

1353
01:12:09,534 --> 01:12:14,330
Now, when it becomes Daichi-san's
featured episode,

1354
01:12:14,414 --> 01:12:16,458
learning his romantic history…

1355
01:12:16,541 --> 01:12:17,667
What happened in his past?

1356
01:12:17,751 --> 01:12:20,587
I'm so curious about that.

1357
01:12:20,670 --> 01:12:21,671
Totally.

1358
01:12:21,963 --> 01:12:23,256
Maybe he was a playboy.

1359
01:12:23,339 --> 01:12:24,424
I don't want that!

1360
01:12:25,800 --> 01:12:26,634
Daichi's X…

1361
01:12:26,718 --> 01:12:29,345
We really don't need that.

1362
01:12:33,433 --> 01:12:38,521
I wonder…

1363
01:12:38,980 --> 01:12:41,775
Do you see me as a woman?

1364
01:12:42,817 --> 01:12:44,277
Do you?

1365
01:12:44,360 --> 01:12:45,236
Me?

1366
01:12:46,279 --> 01:12:47,113
Yes.

1367
01:12:48,114 --> 01:12:50,200
Do you like me as a woman?

1368
01:13:01,169 --> 01:13:03,922
To be honest,

1369
01:13:04,756 --> 01:13:06,591
the biggest reason

1370
01:13:07,675 --> 01:13:09,803
was physical intimacy.
